\par\par \b \uc2 Morning MoneyBeat: What China's Yuan Move Means for the Fed's Liftoff\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kristen Scholer   \par \uc2 1,149 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2015\par 12:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Morning MoneyBeat is the Journal's pre-market primer packed with market updates, insights and must-read news links. To receive this morning newsletter via email, click here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://on.wsj.com/MoneyBeatUSSignup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://on.wsj.com/MoneyBeatUSSignup}}}\par \par \uc2 MARKET SNAP: At 6 a.m. ET, \uc2 S&P 500\uc2  futures up 0.15%. \uc2 Treasury\uc2  yield higher at 2.16%. \uc2 Nymex\uc2  up 0.18% to $43.37; gold 0.57% lower at $1117.2/oz. In Europe, FTSE 100 up 0.71%, DAX up 1.72% and CAC up 1.82%. In Asia, Nikkei 225 up 0.99% and \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  up 0.43%.\par \par \uc2 WATCH FOR: 8:30 a.m. EDT. Weekly Jobless Claims. [Expected 270,000 vs. 270,000 in previous week.]; 8:30 a.m. EDT. July Retail Sales. [Expected 0.6% vs. -0.3% in June.]; 8:30 a.m. EDT. July Import Prices. [Expected -1.1% vs. -0.1% in June.] 10 a.m. EDT. June Business Inventories. [Expected 0.4% vs. 0.3% in May.]\par \par \uc2 THE BREAKFAST BRIEFING\par \par \uc2 China's tumult hasn't dissuaded Wall Street of its view that liftoff could come this September...at least not yet.\par \par \uc2 "So far--all good for staying on track for September," said William Lee, head of North America economics at \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, devaluing the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for two straight days, it sent a chill through U.S. stocks. The Dow Jones Industrial Average lost 1.2% Tuesday and was down as much as 1.6%, or 277 points, Wednesday before recovering to end flat on the session.\par \par \uc2 "People are beginning to realize the move in China may not be as panicky as everyone thought," said Art Cashin, UBS director of floor \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the \uc2 NYSE\uc2 . "[The] primary concern is whether [Chinese] leaders are sophisticated or adept enough to work through that process without accidentally tipping something over."\par \par \uc2 China's move to depreciate the yuan comes as the world's second-largest economy continues to slow and the Shanghai Composite remains 25% below its June 12 high after it lost roughly a third of its value in less than a month.\par \par \uc2 The big question for U.S. investors is what impact China's moves will have on the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's decision to raise the federal-funds rate.\par \par \uc2 Of course, a weaker Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stronger U.S. dollar could keep a lid on inflation, which is already trending below the Fed's 2% objective.\par \par \uc2 Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases borrowing costs, it wants to be reasonably confident that inflation will move back to 2% over the medium term. But, if the greenback appreciates further, it will put downward pressure on import prices and broader inflation.\par \par \uc2 Economists at \uc2 Goldman Sachs Group Inc\uc2 . say the unexpected devaluation of the yuan should only have a small impact on U.S. growth and inflation at this stage. The bank estimates that for every five percentage point increase in the Trade Weighted U.S. Dollar Index, between 0.1 and 0.2 percentage points would be subtracted from year-over-year core inflation.\par \par \uc2 Since the Fed's June meeting, Goldman has called for liftoff in December. Economists there said China's move this week to depreciate its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  only "marginally lowers the odds" of a September increase.\par \par \uc2 While China breathed a bit of uncertainty into markets this week, Wall Street thinks a September liftoff remains in play as it views possible spillover effects to be contained for now.\par \par \uc2 Morning MoneyBeat Daily Factoid: On this day in 1961, East German soldiers began laying down barbed wire and bricks as a barrier between Soviet-controlled East Berlin and the democratic western portion of the city.\par \par \uc2 - By Kristen Scholer\par \par \uc2 STOCKS TO WATCH\par \par \uc2 Nordstrom is projected to report second-quarter earnings of 90 cents a share, according to a survey of analysts by FactSet. The department store company earned 95 cents a share a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 El Pollo Loco\uc2  is forecast to post second-quarter earnings of 18 cents a share, up from 16 cents a share a year ago.\par \par \uc2 Applied Materials\uc2  is expected to post fiscal third-quarter earnings of 33 cents a share, up from 28 cents a share a year ago.\par \par \uc2 MUST READS (LINKS)\par \par \uc2 China Defends Handling of Yuan Plunge: \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials offered a rare public defense after their unexpected move this week to devalue the yuan, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stabilize and eventually resume its climb.\par \par \uc2 Global Markets Rally After Two-Day Tumble: Global markets are rallying after two days of sharp declines following China's unexpected move to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Cheaper Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Has Global Impact: Beijing signaled with its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation that the domestic economic slowdown it has failed to reverse is no longer a problem confined within China's borders. It is now the world's problem, too.\par \par \uc2 Surge in Commercial Real-Estate Prices Stirs Bubble Worries: Investors are pushing commercial real-estate prices to record levels in cities around the world, fueling concerns that the global property market is overheating.\par \par \uc2 Global Gold Demand Drops 12%: Global demand for gold plummeted 12% to a six-year low in the second quarter, as vital buyers in Asia lost their appetite for the metal, the \uc2 World Gold Council\uc2  said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Kraft Heinz to Slash 2,500 Jobs: Kraft Heinz said it will cut 2,500 jobs, including 700 at its Illinois headquarters, as it begins the process of integrating after its merger.\par \par \uc2 Alibaba Hits Record Low, Taking Chinese Internet Stocks Down With It: \uc2 Alibaba Group Holding Ltd\uc2 . is sinking, and it's taking other Chinese internet stocks lower too.\par \par \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  Employees Charged in Emissions Trading Case : Frankfurt's public prosecutor's office has filed charges against eight current and former employees of \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  for the alleged evasion of taxes on trading carbon-emission certificates.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's 'Bad Bank' Isn't So Bad Anymore: Citi Holdings, the "bad bank" \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  created to dispose of unwanted assets, has become a surprise success story.\par \par \uc2 5 Things to Look for in Eurozone GDP: Did the eurozone economy shift down a gear in the second quarter, as some economists fear, or did it manage to hold on to its modest first-quarter performance? We'll find out Friday, when \uc2 Eurostat\uc2  is due to publish GDP estimates.\par \par \uc2 Biden Sounds Out Allies on 2016 Bid: Vice President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  this week is sounding out friends and family about a presidential bid, as some Democrats press him to enter the race.\par \par \uc2 With iPad Sales Falling, Apple Pushes Into Businesses: \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2 ., grappling with swooning sales of the once-blockbuster iPad and sensing an opening in the changing ways of work, is making its broadest assault to date on business computing. \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 13, 2015 06:13 ET (10:13 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150813eb8d00191\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
