\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan ends weaker for 3rd day, c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2015\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Aug 13 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan fell for a third\par straight day on Thursday to a fresh 4-year low, but traders said\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-owned banks to limit\par losses and ease global fears that Beijing may be considering a\par deeper devaluation.\par     Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to have been caught\par off guard by the intensity of selling that was sparked off by\par its surprise 2 percent devaluation on Tuesday, and believe it\par ordered big state banks to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late on\par Wednesday. State banks were also believed to be buying on\par Thursday to stem declines.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.4010 per dollar prior to market open, weaker than the\par previous fix of 6.3306 but near the prior market close. The\par weaker fixing follows through on its commitment to set the\par midpoint with a closer eye on the previous day's closing rate,\par seen as making the fixing more responsive to market forces. \par     The spot market closed at 6.3990 per dollar,\par weakening 0.2 percent from the previous close and has\par depreciated 3 percent since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devalued the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  moved to calm markets again on Thursday, saying\par there was no basis for further depreciation of the yuan given\par the country's strong economic fundamentals, ample \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves and a trade\par surplus.  \par     It signalled it believed the yuan had found its proper new\par level and sources told Reuters it stepped up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par trading by ordering state banks to buy yuan at designated rates\par on behalf of the monetary authorities. \par     "Some major, sporadic transactions emerged today, suspected\par coming from state banks to help the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  to support the yuan,"\par said a trader at a European bank in Shanghai.\par     "They concentrated at 6.43-6.44 per dollar, implying that is\par roughly the line where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  thinks the yuan should\par not fall below in the near term."\par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade with a range 2\par percent above or below the official fixing on any given day, and\par had been trading far weaker than the midpoint for months until\par Tuesday's sudden adjustment.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials denied suggestions that they were\par preparing to push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down 10 percent in order to\par support exports. \par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.76 percent weaker than the\par onshore spot at 6.448 per dollar. \par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par  ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.401    6.3306    -1.10%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.399    6.387     -0.19%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    -0.03%             \par  midpoint*                            