\par\par \b \uc2 China's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Defends Handling of Yuan Plunge\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anjani Trivedi   \par \uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2015\par 07:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 In a rare news conference on Thursday, \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials defended their handling of this week's downward plunge in the yuan and reiterated that they see no reason for it to fall much further.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  officials said the yuan would strengthen again once the market stabilizes, and said they see "no basis" for further depreciation.\par \par \uc2 But investors have a different interpretation of Beijing's move to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 1.9% on Tuesday and its attempt to give the market more sway in its trading level. Many expect a prolonged depreciation of the yuan and forecast bigger price swings as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seeks to engineer its controlled weakening.\par \par \uc2 In early trading Thursday, traders pushed the yuan down as much as 0.9% from its previous close to 6.4470 against the U.S. dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  held steady at 6.4076 through the early afternoon, as investors assess Beijing's latest commentary.\par \par \uc2 "It's going to be a period of volatility for the next few months before [the yuan] finds it equilibrium level," as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows market forces to play a larger role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Alexandra Edstein, senior portfolio manager at London-based hedge fund The Cambridge Strategy's Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund. "The trend will be depreciation," she said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to take into account Wednesday's closing price when setting the yuan's daily trading level. China allows the yuan to trade in a 2% band around its daily fix.\par \par \uc2 It set the yuan at 6.4010 against the U.S. dollar, down just 0.2% from the previous close and 1.1% weaker than Wednesday's fixing. Still, that closing price reflects a late-afternoon surge in the yuan on Wednesday, after authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent an excessive fall.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, on Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2  said that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had "exited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " as a routine measure. Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  insisted it has the ability to keep the market in check with China's "ample" \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves--a war chest of nearly $3.7 trillion to influence its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 A weaker yuan risks setting off a wave of capital outflows but Mr. Yi vowed Thursday to ensure "orderly" cross-border capital flows. He also said capital inflows and outflows were "basically balanced."\par \par \uc2 Officials also pledged to open the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, currently dominated by domestic banks, to "qualified" foreign institutions and extend \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading hours. That potential move could help forge the convergence of the yuan's rate in China and the rate of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded outside the mainland. The yuan has traded at a big discount in Hong Kong as opposed to the mainland, reflecting foreign investors' increasingly pessimistic view of China's economy.\par \par \uc2 China will continue to open its capital account on its own timetable, which won't be affected by outside factors, Mr. Yi said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Anjani Trivedi at anjani.trivedi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 13, 2015 01:20 ET (05:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150813eb8d000gc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
