\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China central bank \highlight\uc2  says halts 'regular' yuan  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , will manage volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao and Pete Sweeney   \par \uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2015\par 10:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 BEIJING (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stopped "regularly" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but could still conduct "effective management" of the yuan in cases of extreme volatility, its vice governor said, as policymakers tried to stem selling this week.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  stunned global markets on Tuesday by suddenly allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall by nearly 2 percent after a run of poor economic data. It fell again on Wednesday, sparking market fears that Beijing was intent on a much deeper devaluation which could destabilize the global economy.\par \par \uc2 PBOC Governor \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2 , who also runs the \uc2 State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was asked at a news conference on Thursday if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  behind closed doors to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already withdrawn from regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Yi said.\par \par \uc2 But he added that the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  will implement "effective management" of the exchange rate in case of external shocks or extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility.\par \par \uc2 However, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  now appears to be moving to stem the slide and calm jittery markets.\par \par \uc2 Trading sources said that major state banks had been buying up yuan and selling off dollars to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , causing the exchange rate to recover sharply in the last few minutes of trade on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 PBOC Assistant Governor Zhang Xiaohui said at the same news conference that the recent decline of the yuan had released "accumulated" depreciation pressure of around 3 percent, adding that loosening monetary policy has added to downward pressure on the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Zhang said the yuan could return to appreciation in the future.\par \par \uc2 NO SHARP YUAN FALLS\par \par \uc2 The officials' comments came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  distributed an official statement in which it said there is no basis for further depreciation in the yuan <CNY=CFXS> given strong economic fundamentals, but that it will increase monitoring of "abnormal" cross-border flows.\par \par \uc2 The officials said that reports suggesting the government could allow the yuan to fall 10 percent were "unfounded" and that there was no need to adjust the exchange rate to support exports.\par \par \uc2 Yi said a more flexible yuan will help make the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy more independent and effective.\par \par \uc2 "This helps expand the room for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make adjustments in interest rates, liquidity and money supply," Yi said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut rates four times since November and also trimmed bank reserve requirements to support flagging growth in the world's second-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to open up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to foreign investors and extend market trading hours to help unify onshore and offshore yuan exchange rates, Yi said.\par \par \uc2 China will follow its own timetable in making the yuan convertible on the capital account, he said without elaborating.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was under pressure from factions within the government to deeply devalue the yuan in order to support struggling exporters.\par \par \uc2 Chinese steelmakers, suffering from endemic overcapacity and weak demand at home, have already leapt to cut prices to boost offshore demand.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts see the yuan depreciating further this year.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Yao, Pete Sweeney and Engen Tham; Editing by \uc2 Jacqueline Wong\uc2  & Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-13T08:54:43.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150813eb8d004h6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
