\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2015\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan June Core Machinery Orders Fall 7.9% on Month \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese core machinery orders fell 7.9% in June from the previous month, the first drop in four months, the government said Thursday, amid growing caution about the global economy with a slowdown in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and weak commodity prices. (published 2359 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China Intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to Support Tumbling Yuan--update \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , after allowing it to fall sharply for two days, shows how the leadership is struggling as it enters largely uncharted territory. (published 2353 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par New Zealand House Prices Still Pushing Higher, Says Reinz \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's housing market remained strong in July. (published 0005 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par New Zealand's July Food Prices Up 1.2% On Year \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's food-price index rose 0.6% in July and 1.2% on the year, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Statistics New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 2254 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par New Zealand's Manufacturing Sector Maintains Solid Pace \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's manufacturing sector eased in July on month but remains in expansionary territory. (published 2249 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par Fed Funds Future Closer To Reality -- Heard On The Street \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When it starts tightening monetary policy, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will likely raise its target range on overnight rates by a very modest quarter of a percentage point. But interest rates themselves may rise by even less than that. (published 2244 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 12 Aug 2015 23:00 ET \par News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Says It Is Equipped to Keep Yuan Stable \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday it has the ability to maintain a stable yuan, while pledging to open the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to foreign investors. (published 0240 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  Holds Rate Steady \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday kept its benchmark interest rate unchanged at a record-low 1.50% for a second straight month as widely expected. (published 0057 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par New Zealand House Prices Still Pushing Higher, Says Reinz \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's housing market remained strong in July. (published 0005 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 13 Aug 2015 02:00 ET \par News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Defends Handling of Yuan Plunge \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a rare news conference on Thursday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials defended their handling of this week's downward plunge in the yuan and reiterated that they see no reason for it to fall much further. (published 0505 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Malaysia 2Q Current-Account Surplus Shrinks 24% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's current-account surplus shrank 24% in the second quarter to 7.6 billion ringgit, mainly due to a lower surplus in the goods account and a higher deficit in services account, the Department of Statistics said Thursday. (published 0502 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Malaysia 2Q GDP Expands 4.9% on Year; Above View \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's economic growth decelerated in the second quarter as exports plunged and domestic demand cooled following the introduction of a consumption tax. (published 0400 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par New Zealand Minister Shrugs off Worries About Yuan Devaluation \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Bill English played down worries that China's devaluation of the yuan would hurt New Zealand exporters, in particular already beleaguered dairy exporters. (published 0513 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Markets Test China's Vow to Ease Grip on Yuan -- update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China guided its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower for a third day Thursday after briefly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop it up the day before, showing how the leadership is struggling to manage the market in largely uncharted territory for Beijing. (published 0314 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  Holds Rate Steady \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday kept its benchmark interest rate unchanged at a record-low 1.50% for a second straight month as widely expected. (published 0057 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par New Zealand House Prices Still Pushing Higher, Says Reinz \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's housing market remained strong in July. (published 0005 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 13, 2015 02:00 ET (06:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150813eb8d0004d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
