\par\par \b \uc2 China \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Capable of Stabilizing Yuan Exchange Rate - \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Economist - Report\b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2015\par 03:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is fully capable of stabilizing the yuan's exchange rate and the recent market fluctuations are controllable, Ma Jun, the chief economist at the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  was cited as saying.\par \par \uc2 "I believe the yuan's fluctuations of the last two days were within a manageable scope," he said in an interview with the Financial News, a newspaper backed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "But more importantly the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is fully capable of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when necessary to stabilize the exchange rate...," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been closely monitoring the market situation since the change in the parity system, or reference rate, for the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 That move on Tuesday effectively devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by nearly 2% and shook financial markets around the world.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Ma also said that China has no intention of setting off a round of competitive devaluations, adding that the yuan's exchange rate is near equilibrium and there is no need for a large depreciation.\par \par \uc2 He also said that although the nation's exports fell 8% in July, there was no reason to over-analyze the statistics for a single month and the decline reflected a number of factors.\par \par \uc2 He added that the Chinese economy should be able to reach the government's growth target of about 7% this year.\par \par \uc2 Write to William Kazer at William.Kazer@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 12, 2015 21:31 ET (01:31 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150813eb8d00027\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
