\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Financial Services News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 16:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO SUPPORT TUMBLING YUAN \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yuan, just a day after it had let it decline sharply, underscoring the tricky balancing act now facing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FIS TO BUY FINANCIAL-TECH FIRM SUNGARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fidelity National agreed to buy financial software company \f28 \uc2 \f2 SunGard\f28 \uc2 \f2  for $9.1 billion, including the assumption of debt, ending its plans to go public. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHINA'S NEIGHBORS FEEL PAIN OF YUAN DEVALUATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The blowback from the China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation is being felt most directly in the financial markets on the country's periphery, where governments and central banks scrambled to respond. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DUDLEY: MONETARY POLICY ALONE CAN'T SOLVE LABOR MARKET STRUCTURAL IMBALANCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York President \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Dudley\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday highlighted structural imbalances in the labor market, saying they cannot be resolved with monetary policy alone. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par COMMONWEALTH BANK PLANS $3.7 BILLION CAPITAL BOOST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's biggest bank is tapping investors for about $3.7 billion, joining fellow lenders in turning to shareholders to top up capital buffers to meet new regulatory requirements. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GREECE FACES TWO-YEAR RECESSION AMID BAILOUT CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The country's economy is expected to shrink 2.3% this year, followed by a 1.3% contraction next year, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MARKIT EDGES ABOVE EARNINGS, REVENUE FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial-data provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 Markit Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . edged above Wall Street forecasts for earnings and sales in its latest quarter as the company offset \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  headwinds with new business and acquisitions in its systems and software unit. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PUERTO RICO INVESTORS WIN RELIEF FROM \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mom-and-pop investors facing steep losses in Puerto Rico municipal-bond funds are starting to get some money back, following legal victories against the unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  that sold the funds \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INSIDE SOFTBANK'S STRUGGLE TO TURN AROUND SPRINT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two years after a takeover, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Masayoshi Son\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief executive of SoftBank, has pushed hard for changes at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sprint\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which needs a massive overhaul to stay competitive. But it just slipped into last place in subscribers among the four major U.S. mobile operators. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GOLDMAN TO GIVE OUT 'SECRET SAUCE' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a major shift for the New York investment bank, Goldman officials say they are preparing to offer clients access to some of its tools for analyzing markets and managing risk. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CREDIT SUISSE\f28 \uc2 \f2 , BARCLAYS IN TALKS TO SETTLE 'DARK POOL' ALLEGATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 , two of the biggest operators of "dark pools," have entered settlement negotiations with the New York attorney general and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Securities and Exchange Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  over allegations of wrongdoing in the private trading venues. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GE\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SELL HEALTH-CARE LENDING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 CAPITAL ONE\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GE\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it has reached an agreement to sell $8.5 billion of health-care related loans and its health-care financial services lending business to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capital One\f28 \uc2 \f2  for about $9 billion. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BANKS REDISCOVER THEIR HOMING INSTINCT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The long-term trend of banks unloading mortgages has reversed, which should bolster earnings but could hurt \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fannie Mae\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Freddie Mac\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 12, 2015 10:02 ET (14:02 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c001z4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
