\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Financial Services News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. APPEALS RULING IN \f28 \uc2 \f2 AIG\f28 \uc2 \f2  BAILOUT DISPUTE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday filed to appeal a judge's ruling that it violated the law when it took a controlling stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 AIG\f28 \uc2 \f2  in 2008. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLS FARGO MORTGAGE\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXECUTIVE MICHAEL HEID TO RETIRE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Michael Heid\f28 \uc2 \f2  will retire this fall as head of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo\f28 \uc2 \f2 's mortgage business, the country's largest by volume. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CITIZENS BANK FINED FOR MISHANDLING DEPOSITS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citizens Financial Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has been ordered to pay $31.5 million for at times failing to credit the full amount of money customers deposited into their accounts. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WHY CHINA IS SCARING INVESTORS IN U.S. BANK STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banks stocks are taking a beating Wednesday. The reason: China and new uncertainty over when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  might raise rates. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ITG CONFIRMS PLAN TO PAY $20 MILLION TO SETTLE SEC DARK POOL CHARGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ITG confirmed it plans to pay $20.3 million to settle allegations that it operated a secret trading desk and misused confidential trading information. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GOLDMAN TO GIVE OUT 'SECRET SAUCE' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a major shift for the New York investment bank, Goldman officials say they are preparing to offer clients access to some of its tools for analyzing markets and managing risk. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FIS TO BUY SUNGARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fidelity National agreed to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 SunGard\f28 \uc2 \f2  for $5.1 billion in cash and stock, a decade after a group of private-equity firms acquired the financial software company in one of the signature deals of the buyout boom.. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par COMMONWEALTH BANK PLANS $3.7 BILLION CAPITAL BOOST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's biggest bank is tapping investors for about $3.7 billion, joining fellow lenders in turning to shareholders to top up capital buffers to meet new regulatory requirements. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MARKETS TEST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S VOW TO EASE GRIP \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yuan just a day after it had let it decline sharply, underscoring the tricky balancing act now facing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DUDLEY: CHINA MOVES HAVE 'HUGE IMPLICATIONS,' BUT FED APPEARS ON TRACK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York President \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Dudley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have "huge implications for the world economy" but the U.S. appears on track to raise short-term interest rates in the near future. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GREECE FACES TWO-YEAR RECESSION AMID BAILOUT CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The country's economy is expected to shrink 2.3% this year, followed by a 1.3% contraction next year, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.K. BANKS' ECONOMIC WEIGHT DEMANDS RULES STAY STRICT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  will review how new regulations might affect growth, but that won't mean big changes. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHINA'S NEIGHBORS FEEL PAIN OF YUAN DEVALUATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The blowback from the China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation is being felt most directly in the financial markets on the country's periphery, where governments and central banks scrambled to respond. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MARKIT EDGES ABOVE EARNINGS, REVENUE FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial-data provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 Markit Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . edged above Wall Street forecasts for earnings and sales in its latest quarter as the company offset \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  headwinds with new business and acquisitions in its systems and software unit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 12, 2015 16:01 ET (20:01 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c00326\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
