\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 23:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. STOCKS STAGE LATE RALLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks staged an afternoon rally to recover from a second day of losses following China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation, though investors remained unsettled over the implications of the sudden shift in the second-largest world economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MARKETS TEST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S VOW TO EASE GRIP \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yuan just a day after it had let it decline sharply, underscoring the tricky balancing act now facing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CISCO\f28 \uc2 \f2  REVENUE AND PROFIT GROW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cisco Systems Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s recent growth pace eased a bit in the latest quarter, but the network-equipment giant and its new chief executive said the company's recent rebound remains on track. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MADOFF FEEDER FUND LAWSUIT MAY PROCEED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A lawsuit seeking to reclaim $825 million from two major funds that invested with Bernard Madoff may move forward largely intact, a bankruptcy judge ruled Tuesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SPENDING BATTLE LOOMS EVEN AS DEFICIT SHRINKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. budget deficit rose in July but stood around 9% below its year-earlier level, the Treasury Department said on Wednesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MACY'S\f28 \uc2 \f2  CUTS GUIDANCE AS SALES, PROFIT SLIDE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macy's\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its forecast for sales growth this year to zero after posting a drop in earnings, intensifying pressure on the retailer to find new ways to grow beyond its core department-store business. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KRAFT HEINZ TO SLASH 2,500 JOBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kraft Heinz said it will cut 2,500 jobs, including 700 at its Illinois headquarters, as it begins the process of integrating after its merger. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HUGE BLAST KILLS AT LEAST SEVEN IN CHINESE PORT CITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A huge explosion rocked the northern Chinese port city of Tianjin late Wednesday, killing at least seven people and injuring at least 50, while sending flames and a plume of smoke high into the sky. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  DEFENDS \f28 \uc2 \f2 DIRECTV\f28 \uc2 \f2  ACQUISITION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Randall Stephenson\f28 \uc2 \f2  launched a robust defense of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 DirecTV\f28 \uc2 \f2  acquisition that has been criticized as ill-timed in the face of rapid declines in cable television subscriptions. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. APPEALS RULING IN \f28 \uc2 \f2 AIG\f28 \uc2 \f2  BAILOUT DISPUTE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday filed to appeal a judge's ruling that it violated the law when it took a controlling stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 AIG\f28 \uc2 \f2  in 2008. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WESTERN DIGITAL CHAIRMAN \f28 \uc2 \f2 TOM PARDUN\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO RETIRE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Western Digital Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday that chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tom Pardun\f28 \uc2 \f2  will retire in November, having reached the mandatory retirement age. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PURE STORAGE, VALUED AT ABOUT $3 BILLION, FILES FOR IPO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pure Storage Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a data-storage startup valued privately at roughly $3 billion, filed to go public in what may become a crush of IPOs by business-technology firms. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PETROBRAS MAY SELL STAKE IN FUEL-DISTRIBUTION BUSINESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's state-run oil company Petr\u243\'00\'F3 leo Brasileiro is in talks with three potential buyers interested in purchasing a stake in its fuel distribution business before a planned initial public offering of that unit. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DUDLEY: CHINA MOVES HAVE 'HUGE IMPLICATIONS,' BUT FED APPEARS ON TRACK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York President \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Dudley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have "huge implications for the world economy" but the U.S. appears on track to raise short-term interest rates in the near future. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. JOB OPENINGS IN JUNE FALL A BIT FROM RECORD HIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of job openings in the U.S. fell slightly in June, though the overall level suggests demand for workers remains strong. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par REALITY HITS ALIBABA'S RESULTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Months after its blockbuster U.S. IPO, Alibaba reported its slowest quarterly revenue growth in more than three years, while its transactions with Chinese consumers also disappointed. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CORN, SOYBEAN PRICES DROP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corn and soybean prices plunged Wednesday after federal forecasters raised their outlook for the U.S. harvest this autumn, surprising analysts. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GREECE FACES TWO-YEAR RECESSION AMID BAILOUT CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The country's economy is expected to shrink 2.3% this year, followed by a 1.3% contraction next year, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ITG CONFIRMS PLAN TO PAY $20 MILLION TO SETTLE SEC DARK POOL CHARGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ITG confirmed it plans to pay $20.3 million to settle allegations that it operated a secret trading desk and misused confidential trading information. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SENIOR EXECUTIVE \f28 \uc2 \f2 TIM KILPIN\f28 \uc2 \f2  LEAVING \f28 \uc2 \f2 MATTEL\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mattel\f28 \uc2 \f2  is losing one of its top executives at a time when the struggling toy maker is trying to spark its creative culture and end a long string of poor results. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par  \par Heard on the Street \par FED FUNDS FUTURE NEARER THAN YOU THINK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The mechanics of how the Fed will raise rates after years of easing means the chances of it acting next month are likely higher than many think. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Business \par U.S. FARMS STRUGGLE TO FIND WORKERS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. farm companies, in dire need of people to harvest fruits and vegetables, are raising wages and enhancing medical and other benefits. Even so, a worsening labor shortage is reducing fruit and vegetable production by an estimated 9.5%, or $3.1 billion, a year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 12, 2015 17:00 ET (21:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c003gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
