\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 756 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 23:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. STOCKS STAGE LATE RALLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks staged an afternoon rally to recover from a second day of losses following China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation, though investors remained unsettled over the implications of the sudden shift in the second-largest world economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MARKETS TEST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S VOW TO EASE GRIP \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yuan just a day after it had let it decline sharply, underscoring the tricky balancing act now facing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CISCO\f28 \uc2 \f2  REVENUE AND PROFIT GROW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cisco Systems Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s recent growth pace eased a bit in the latest quarter, but the network-equipment giant and its new chief executive said the company's recent rebound remains on track. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MADOFF FEEDER FUND LAWSUIT MAY PROCEED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A lawsuit seeking to reclaim $825 million from two major funds that invested with Bernard Madoff may move forward largely intact, a bankruptcy judge ruled Tuesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPENDING BATTLE LOOMS EVEN AS DEFICIT SHRINKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. budget deficit rose in July but stood around 9% below its year-earlier level, the Treasury Department said on Wednesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MACY'S\f28 \uc2 \f2  CUTS GUIDANCE AS SALES, PROFIT SLIDE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macy's\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its forecast for sales growth this year to zero after posting a drop in earnings, intensifying pressure on the retailer to find new ways to grow beyond its core department-store business. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KRAFT HEINZ TO SLASH 2,500 JOBS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kraft Heinz said it will cut 2,500 jobs, including 700 at its Illinois headquarters, as it begins the process of integrating after its merger. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUGE BLAST KILLS AT LEAST SEVEN IN CHINESE PORT CITY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A huge explosion rocked the northern Chinese port city of Tianjin late Wednesday, killing at least seven people and injuring at least 50, while sending flames and a plume of smoke high into the sky. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  DEFENDS \f28 \uc2 \f2 DIRECTV\f28 \uc2 \f2  ACQUISITION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Randall Stephenson\f28 \uc2 \f2  launched a robust defense of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 DirecTV\f28 \uc2 \f2  acquisition that has been criticized as ill-timed in the face of rapid declines in cable television subscriptions. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. APPEALS RULING IN \f28 \uc2 \f2 AIG\f28 \uc2 \f2  BAILOUT DISPUTE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday filed to appeal a judge's ruling that it violated the law when it took a controlling stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 AIG\f28 \uc2 \f2  in 2008. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Heard on the Street \par FED FUNDS FUTURE NEARER THAN YOU THINK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The mechanics of how the Fed will raise rates after years of easing means the chances of it acting next month are likely higher than many think. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Business \par U.S. FARMS STRUGGLE TO FIND WORKERS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. farm companies, in dire need of people to harvest fruits and vegetables, are raising wages and enhancing medical and other benefits. Even so, a worsening labor shortage is reducing fruit and vegetable production by an estimated 9.5%, or $3.1 billion, a year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Capital Account \par BEYOND THE INTERNET, INNOVATION STRUGGLES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2 's reorganization highlights an overlooked reason why productivity is struggling-the transformative and profitable innovations in the Internet, technology and media are glaringly absent in the rest of the economy, writes Greg Ip. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Ahead of the Tape \par NORDSTROM TRIES TO DODGE THE BARGAIN BIN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordstrom is riding high but disappointment at rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macy's\f28 \uc2 \f2  and a premium valuation make the stock vulnerable. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par U.S. STOCKS STAGE LATE RALLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks staged an afternoon rally to recover from a second day of losses following China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation, though investors remained unsettled over the implications of the sudden shift in the second-largest world economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. GOVERNMENT\f28 \uc2 \f2  BONDS PARE PRICE GAINS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Demand for ultrasafe \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  debt sent the yield on the benchmark 10-year note to the lowest level in more than three months. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DOLLAR WEAKENS ON GROWING FEARS OF FED DELAY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar tumbled against the euro and the yen on Wednesday as the picture for U.S. interest rates muddied for more investors after China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plunged for a second day. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OIL PRICES BOUNCE, GASOLINE SOARS ON STRONG SIGNS FOR DEMAND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices pared gains after a report showed U.S. stockpiles shrinking less than expected, but the market remained buoyant from international data showing a rapid increase in demand. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GOLD HIT NEW RECENT HIGH AS STOCKS FALL ON CHINA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices rose to their highest level in about three weeks Wednesday, as investors fled to the safe-haven metal after China's devaluation roiled markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 12, 2015 17:00 ET (21:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c003h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
