\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 19:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. STOCKS DOWN ON CHINA, EARNINGS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks declined Wednesday, weighed down by a batch of disappointing corporate earnings and continued worries about the pace of growth in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO SUPPORT TUMBLING YUAN \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yuan, just a day after it had let it decline sharply, underscoring the tricky balancing act now facing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BASE METALS CRASH TO FRESH LOWS ON YUAN DEVALUATION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 London base metals tumbled to new multiyear lows as China's further devaluation of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spooked risk-averse investors into selling the commodities that the world's second-largest economy had been buying in bulk. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MACY'S\f28 \uc2 \f2  CUTS GUIDANCE AS SALES, PROFIT SLIDE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macy's\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its forecast for sales growth this year to zero after posting a drop in earnings, intensifying pressure on the retailer to find new ways to grow beyond its core department-store business. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KRAFT HEINZ TO SLASH 2,500 JOBS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kraft Heinz said it will cut 2,500 jobs, including 700 at its Illinois headquarters, as it begins the process of integrating after its merger. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DUDLEY: CHINA MOVES HAVE 'HUGE IMPLICATIONS,' BUT FED APPEARS ON TRACK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York President \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Dudley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have "huge implications for the world economy" but the U.S. appears on track to raise short-term interest rates in the near future. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par REALITY HITS ALIBABA'S RESULTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Months after its blockbuster U.S. IPO, Alibaba reported its slowest quarterly revenue growth in more than three years, while its transactions with Chinese consumers also disappointed. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  GIVES GUIDANCE FOR \f28 \uc2 \f2 DIRECTV\f28 \uc2 \f2  ERA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  laid out guidance through 2018 ahead of a conference with analysts, giving a peek at what its financials will look like following its tie-up with \f28 \uc2 \f2 DirecTV\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HEWLETT-PACKARD\f28 \uc2 \f2  NAMES POST-BREAKUP BOARD MEMBERS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hewlett-Packard Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Wednesday named current and former executives at companies like \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Motors Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Comcast Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to sit on the boards of the two companies it will split into in November \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITG CONFIRMS PLAN TO PAY $20 MILLION TO SETTLE SEC DARK POOL CHARGES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ITG confirmed it plans to pay $20.3 million to settle allegations that it operated a secret trading desk and misused confidential trading information. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Business \par U.S. FARMS STRUGGLE TO FIND WORKERS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. farm companies, in dire need of people to harvest fruits and vegetables, are raising wages and enhancing medical and other benefits. Even so, a worsening labor shortage is reducing fruit and vegetable production by an estimated 9.5%, or $3.1 billion, a year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Moneybeat Blog \par IS \f28 \uc2 \f2 GOOGLE\f28 \uc2 \f2  REALLY BECOMING THE '\f28 \uc2 \f2 BERKSHIRE HATHAWAY\f28 \uc2 \f2  OF THE INTERNET'? \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  is undergoing a massive restructuring that has it embracing the conglomerate model. But is it fair to compare it to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Warren Buffett\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Berkshire Hathaway\f28 \uc2 \f2 ? We can see the arguments for both "yes" and "no." \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Asia News \par CHINA'S NEIGHBORS FEEL PAIN OF YUAN DEVALUATION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The blowback from the China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation is being felt most directly in the financial markets on the country's periphery, where governments and central banks scrambled to respond. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Heard on the Street \par ALIBABA MANIA CONTINUES TO FADE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alibaba's decline looks set to continue after the once high-flying e-commerce giant reported an underwhelming quarter. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par U.S. STOCKS DOWN ON CHINA, EARNINGS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks declined Wednesday, weighed down by a batch of disappointing corporate earnings and continued worries about the pace of growth in China. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par YUAN JITTERS SEND INVESTORS TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. GOVERNMENT\f28 \uc2 \f2  BONDS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds strengthened Wednesday, sending the yield on the benchmark 10-year note to the lowest level in more than three months, as concerns over China boosted demand for haven assets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DOLLAR WEAKENS ON GROWING FEARS OF FED DELAY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar tumbled against the euro and the yen on Wednesday as the picture for U.S. interest rates muddied for more investors after China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plunged for a second day. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OIL PRICES PARE GAINS, BUT STILL ON REBOUND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices pared gains after a report showed U.S. stockpiles shrinking less than expected, but the market remained buoyant from international data showing a rapid increase in demand. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GOLD HIT NEW RECENT HIGH AS STOCKS FALL ON CHINA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices rose to their highest level in about three weeks Wednesday, as investors fled to the safe-haven metal after China's devaluation roiled markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 12, 2015 13:12 ET (17:12 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c002mw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
