\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 858 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 19:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. STOCKS DOWN ON CHINA, EARNINGS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks declined Wednesday, weighed down by a batch of disappointing corporate earnings and continued worries about the pace of growth in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO SUPPORT TUMBLING YUAN \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yuan, just a day after it had let it decline sharply, underscoring the tricky balancing act now facing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BASE METALS CRASH TO FRESH LOWS ON YUAN DEVALUATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 London base metals tumbled to new multiyear lows as China's further devaluation of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spooked risk-averse investors into selling the commodities that the world's second-largest economy had been buying in bulk. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MACY'S\f28 \uc2 \f2  CUTS GUIDANCE AS SALES, PROFIT SLIDE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macy's\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its forecast for sales growth this year to zero after posting a drop in earnings, intensifying pressure on the retailer to find new ways to grow beyond its core department-store business. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KRAFT HEINZ TO SLASH 2,500 JOBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kraft Heinz said it will cut 2,500 jobs, including 700 at its Illinois headquarters, as it begins the process of integrating after its merger. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DUDLEY: CHINA MOVES HAVE 'HUGE IMPLICATIONS,' BUT FED APPEARS ON TRACK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York President \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Dudley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have "huge implications for the world economy" but the U.S. appears on track to raise short-term interest rates in the near future. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par REALITY HITS ALIBABA'S RESULTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Months after its blockbuster U.S. IPO, Alibaba reported its slowest quarterly revenue growth in more than three years, while its transactions with Chinese consumers also disappointed. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  GIVES GUIDANCE FOR \f28 \uc2 \f2 DIRECTV\f28 \uc2 \f2  ERA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  laid out guidance through 2018 ahead of a conference with analysts, giving a peek at what its financials will look like following its tie-up with \f28 \uc2 \f2 DirecTV\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HEWLETT-PACKARD\f28 \uc2 \f2  NAMES POST-BREAKUP BOARD MEMBERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hewlett-Packard Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Wednesday named current and former executives at companies like \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Motors Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Comcast Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to sit on the boards of the two companies it will split into in November \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ITG CONFIRMS PLAN TO PAY $20 MILLION TO SETTLE SEC DARK POOL CHARGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ITG confirmed it plans to pay $20.3 million to settle allegations that it operated a secret trading desk and misused confidential trading information. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FIS TO BUY FINANCIAL-TECH FIRM SUNGARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fidelity National agreed to buy financial software company \f28 \uc2 \f2 SunGard\f28 \uc2 \f2  for $9.1 billion, including the assumption of debt, ending its plans to go public. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GREECE FACES TWO-YEAR RECESSION AMID BAILOUT CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The country's economy is expected to shrink 2.3% this year, followed by a 1.3% contraction next year, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PEARSON SELLS 50% STAKE IN PUBLISHER OF THE ECONOMIST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pearson has agreed to sell its 50% stake in the publisher of the Economist magazine to the unit's existing shareholders for about $730 million in cash, the company's latest move to focus on education. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SMITHFIELD EARNINGS DROP 27% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Smithfield Foods\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported a 27% decline in second-quarter profit as the world's largest hog producer struggled against low pork prices and the rising U.S. dollar. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ARAMARK\f28 \uc2 \f2  REPORTS 28% DECLINE IN PROFIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aramark\f28 \uc2 \f2  said profit slid in its latest quarter, driven by a sales decline in its North American food and support-services segment. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ALIBABA, TENCENT PLAN TO INVEST IN STARTUP IN RARE ALLIANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Tencent are in talks to invest in China Media Capital's Internet-TV startup in a rare collaboration between the two major Chinese rivals. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FEDEX\f28 \uc2 \f2  NOT CONCERNED BY EU PROBE INTO TNT TAKEOVER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The delivery company is not looking at possible remedies to eliminate the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2 's antitrust concerns, EMEA President \f28 \uc2 \f2 David Binks\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in an interview with The Wall Street Journal. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HOME-SEARCH COMPANY ZOOPLA SEES ESTATE AGENTS RETURN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. estate agents have been returning to Internet home-search firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Zoopla Property Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the latest turn in a battle for Britain's online house hunters. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL DEMAND GROWING AT FASTEST PACE IN FIVE YEARS, SAYS IEA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Demand for oil is increasing at its fastest pace in five years, boosted by an oil-price drop below $50 a barrel, a top energy watchdog said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDIA REPORTS UPBEAT INFLATION,  PRODUCTION DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India reported a greater-than-expected slowdown in inflation and an acceleration in industrial production, indicating gathering strength in the economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par  \par Business \par U.S. FARMS STRUGGLE TO FIND WORKERS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. farm companies, in dire need of people to harvest fruits and vegetables, are raising wages and enhancing medical and other benefits. Even so, a worsening labor shortage is reducing fruit and vegetable production by an estimated 9.5%, or $3.1 billion, a year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Moneybeat Blog \par IS \f28 \uc2 \f2 GOOGLE\f28 \uc2 \f2  REALLY BECOMING THE '\f28 \uc2 \f2 BERKSHIRE HATHAWAY\f28 \uc2 \f2  OF THE INTERNET'? \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  is undergoing a massive restructuring that has it embracing the conglomerate model. But is it fair to compare it to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Warren Buffett\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Berkshire Hathaway\f28 \uc2 \f2 ? We can see the arguments for both "yes" and "no." \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 12, 2015 13:12 ET (17:12 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c002ks\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
