\par\par \b \uc2 China Fears Spark Fresh Market Selloff. Here's What the Street Thinks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Phillipa Leighton-Jones and Christopher Whittall   \par \uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 18:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Equities screens are red. The market moved into risk-off mode for the second day Wednesday after China devalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second day in a row, a move that led to a sharp selloff in the yuan and an end-of-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to people familiar with the matter, to prevent a sharper yuan selloff.\par \par \uc2 As the WSJ's chief \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers Jon Hilsenrath and Brian Blackstone report, a cheaper yuan has a global impact: It could help Chinese exporters but hurts foreign ones, while sending a signal to investors that policy makers in China and elsewhere are straining for tools to address the problem of slow growth.\par \par \uc2 "It's sinking in that yesterday's yuan move wasn't a one-off," said Mads Pedersen, head of global asset allocation at \uc2 UBS\uc2  Wealth Management, which oversees around $2 trillion of assets.\par \par \uc2 "A move to a market-based regime should be a positive in the long run, but at the moment that's being overwhelmed by the uncertainty about how far this goes. It's negative for risk assets," he said.\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2  strategists wrote in a note to clients Wednesday that China's move, which could export disinflation, could prompt the market to reconsider how quickly central banks in developed markets would raise rates, a sentiment that is already being discussed in financial markets.\par \par \uc2 They said: "Our view here is driven to a large extent by the fact that China has renewed its efforts to further gain market share at a time when the global trade pie is hardly growing."\par \par \uc2 According to the Fed Fund Future, a futures contract estimating the likelihood of \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  rate rises, the probability of a rate hike in September has fallen from 50% to just a third between last Friday and Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Any disinflationary impact that causes a delay to interest rate raises, they said, could ultimately benefit equities in the developed world, \uc2 UBS\uc2  strategists said.\par \par \uc2 Some investors are already bargain-hunting.\par \par \uc2 "We have had a positive mood in European equity markets up until now. It's clear the slowdown in China now might be a problem for the coming months," said Yves Maillot, head of equities at \uc2 Natixis Global Asset Management\uc2 , which oversees $904 billion in assets.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Maillot said there is room for stock prices to fall further, with potential for declines of 10% to 15% in the worst-hit sectors over the course of a few sessions.\par \par \uc2 However, he said he was bargain hunting in the worst-affected sectors, such as luxury goods, and predicted broader European stock markets should soon stabilize.\par \par \uc2 Frances Hudson, global thematic strategist at \uc2 Standard Life Investments\uc2 , which oversees GBP250 billion ($390 billion) in assets, said equity analysts will be working overtime to reassess the sales and revenues projections of companies with close links to China. "There should be discrimination between individual companies," said Ms. Hudson, rather than the broad-based market selloff that is currently occurring.\par \par \uc2 "The devaluation has been on the cards for a while as a remedy for the things that are ailing China," said Ms. Hudson, but the speed of the devaluation has caught the market unawares, she added.\par \par \uc2 "It could go on for a while. It's looking a little bit like a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war."\par \par \uc2 Here's what China's fresh rate move overnight has done to markets Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 12, 2015 12:05 ET (16:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c002d0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
