\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 820 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 16:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO SUPPORT TUMBLING YUAN \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the yuan, just a day after it had let it decline sharply, underscoring the tricky balancing act now facing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. STOCKS TUMBLE AGAIN ON CHINA WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks opened sharply lower for a second day as investors continued to worry about the pace of growth in China. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  GIVES GUIDANCE FOR \f28 \uc2 \f2 DIRECTV\f28 \uc2 \f2  ERA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AT&T\f28 \uc2 \f2  laid out guidance through 2018 ahead of a conference with analysts, giving a peek at what its financials will look like following its tie-up with \f28 \uc2 \f2 DirecTV\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HEWLETT-PACKARD\f28 \uc2 \f2  NAMES POST-BREAKUP BOARD MEMBERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hewlett-Packard Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Wednesday named current and former executives at companies like \f28 \uc2 \f2 General Motors Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Comcast Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to sit on the boards of the two companies it will split into in November \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MACY'S\f28 \uc2 \f2  CUTS GUIDANCE AS SALES, PROFIT SLIDE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macy's\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its sales guidance for the year after reporting steeper-than-expected slides in sales and profit in its second quarter. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KRAFT HEINZ TO SLASH 2,500 JOBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kraft Heinz said it will cut 2,500 jobs, including 700 at its Illinois headquarters, as it begins the process of integrating after its merger. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDIA REPORTS UPBEAT INFLATION,  PRODUCTION DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India reported a greater-than-expected slowdown in inflation and an acceleration in industrial production, indicating gathering strength in the economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ALIBABA REVENUE DISAPPOINTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alibaba reported a softer-than-expected 28% increase in revenue in its latest quarter, and the Chinese e-commerce giant said it has authorized a $4 billion stock-buyback program. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DUDLEY: MONETARY POLICY ALONE CAN'T SOLVE LABOR MARKET STRUCTURAL IMBALANCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York President \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Dudley\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday highlighted structural imbalances in the labor market, saying they cannot be resolved with monetary policy alone. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FIS TO BUY FINANCIAL-TECH FIRM SUNGARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fidelity National agreed to buy financial software company \f28 \uc2 \f2 SunGard\f28 \uc2 \f2  for $9.1 billion, including the assumption of debt, ending its plans to go public. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ALIBABA, TENCENT PLAN TO INVEST IN STARTUP IN RARE ALLIANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Tencent are in talks to invest in China Media Capital's Internet-TV startup in a rare collaboration between the two major Chinese rivals. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GREECE FACES TWO-YEAR RECESSION AMID BAILOUT CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The country's economy is expected to shrink 2.3% this year, followed by a 1.3% contraction next year, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par VIETNAM WIDENS DONG'S TRADING BAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam doubled the width of the dong's trading band, a day after China pushed the yuan into its biggest devaluation in two decades. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROZONE INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION FALLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial production across the eurozone declined more than expected in June, as output fell in the region's three largest economies, another sign that lackluster investment continues to restrain economic activity. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ARAMARK\f28 \uc2 \f2  REPORTS 28% DECLINE IN PROFIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aramark\f28 \uc2 \f2  said profit slid in its latest quarter, driven by a sales decline in its North American food and support-services segment. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL DEMAND GROWING AT FASTEST PACE IN FIVE YEARS, SAYS IEA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Demand for oil is increasing at its fastest pace in five years, boosted by an oil-price drop below $50 a barrel, a top energy watchdog said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MARKIT EDGES ABOVE EARNINGS, REVENUE FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial-data provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 Markit Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . edged above Wall Street forecasts for earnings and sales in its latest quarter as the company offset \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  headwinds with new business and acquisitions in its systems and software unit. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par COMMONWEALTH BANK PLANS $3.7 BILLION CAPITAL BOOST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's biggest bank is tapping investors for about $3.7 billion, joining fellow lenders in turning to shareholders to top up capital buffers to meet new regulatory requirements. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PEARSON SELLS 50% STAKE IN PUBLISHER OF THE ECONOMIST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pearson has agreed to sell its 50% stake in the publisher of the Economist magazine to the unit's existing shareholders for about $730 million in cash, the company's latest move to focus on education. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 E.ON\f28 \uc2 \f2  HURT BY WEAKER POWER PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 E.ON\f28 \uc2 \f2  has turned a rise in first-half net profit despite weak power and oil prices, as well as the devaluation of the Russian ruble, though its underlying performance betrayed still tough trading conditions for German utilities. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par  \par Asia News \par CHINA'S NEIGHBORS FEEL PAIN OF YUAN DEVALUATION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The blowback from the China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation is being felt most directly in the financial markets on the country's periphery, where governments and central banks scrambled to respond. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Moneybeat Blog \par IS \f28 \uc2 \f2 GOOGLE\f28 \uc2 \f2  REALLY BECOMING THE '\f28 \uc2 \f2 BERKSHIRE HATHAWAY\f28 \uc2 \f2  OF THE INTERNET'? \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  is undergoing a massive restructuring that has it embracing the conglomerate model. But is it fair to compare it to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Warren Buffett\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Berkshire Hathaway\f28 \uc2 \f2 ? We can see the arguments for both "yes" and "no." \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 12, 2015 10:01 ET (14:01 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c0021f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
