\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 15:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China Intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Support Tumbling Yuan\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yuan, just a day after it had let it decline sharply, underscoring the tricky balancing act now facing its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dudley: Monetary Policy Alone Can't Solve Labor Market Structural Imbalances\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York President \uc2 William Dudley\uc2  on Wednesday highlighted structural imbalances in the labor market, saying they cannot be resolved with monetary policy alone.\par \par \uc2 Greece Faces Two-Year Recession Amid Bailout Cuts\par \par \uc2 The country's economy is expected to shrink 2.3% this year, followed by a 1.3% contraction next year, according to \uc2 European Union\uc2  officials.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Sticks to Its Pledge With Yuan Fix\par \par \uc2 China's yuan fell sharply in early trading Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed through on promises to allow the market to play a greater role in setting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's level.\par \par \uc2 China Industrial Production Growth Slows in July\par \par \uc2 China got another dose of largely disappointing economic data as growth in industrial output slowed in July, adding to a raft of indicators pointing to weakness in the world's second-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 IMF\uc2  Welcomes China's Yuan Move\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  called China's move to allow a greater role for market forces in the yuan "a welcome step," but signaled Beijing has much further to go in letting its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam Widens Dong's Trading Band\par \par \uc2 Vietnam doubled the width of the dong's trading band, a day after China pushed the yuan into its biggest devaluation in two decades.\par \par \uc2 Eurozone Industrial Production Falls in June\par \par \uc2 Industrial production across the eurozone declined more than expected in June, as output fell in the region's three largest economies, another sign that lackluster investment continues to restrain economic activity.\par \par \uc2 U.K. Labor Market Shows Signs of Leveling Off\par \par \uc2 Britain's unemployment rate edged up in June and wage growth stayed flat, signs that the jobs market may be beginning to level off after months of strong employment gains.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 12, 2015 09:18 ET (13:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150812eb8c001rj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
