\par\par \b \uc2 BE Aerospace\uc2  Chief Views PCP Price As Low -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2015\par 19:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 13:37 EDT - \uc2 BE Aerospace\uc2  (BEAV) \uc2 Amin Khoury\uc2  joins the chorus expressing surprise at the price offered by \uc2 Berkshire Hathaway\uc2  (BRKB) for \uc2 Precision Castparts\uc2  (PCP). Khoury, who is also chairman of rival aerospace parts specialist KLX, says at an investor conference that his "guess" is PCP's outlook isn't as strong as many analysts and outsiders expected. PCP recently down 8 cents at $230.84, still below the $235 offer price. (doug.cameron@wsj.com; @dougcameron)\par \par \uc2 13:34 EDT - If nothing else, Isle of Capri (ISLE) closing its Natchez, Miss., casino and selling nongaming assets there for $11.5M removes some distraction from the 14-casino regional operator. The facility was the smallest revenue generator for the company last FY at just 1.9% and the only one with an operating loss besides a newly opened facility in Pennsylvania. ISLE bought Natchez in 2000 as part of its acquisition of Lady Luck Gaming. ISLE has ticked up from session lows on the news and is now off 2.5% on the day at $18.52; shares have more than doubled this year. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 13:11 EDT - The risk-off tone in global markets boosts demand for the \uc2 US Treasury\uc2 's $24B sale of 3-year notes, the first leg of this week's new offerings. The new notes sold at a 1.013% yield, in line with dealers' expectations. The indirect bidding, a gauge of foreign demand, jumps to 52.8%, a multi-year high, from 47.7% a month ago. Direct bids pull back to 8.2%, the lowest since March. Three-year notes are among the most vulnerable if the Fed raises rates, so the strong demand comes as China's yuan devaluation overnight casts doubt over potential Fed tightening next month. Ten-year yield near session lows at 2.119%. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 13:07 EDT - While many in the markets believe the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  devalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost exports, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have acted to ward off the effects of an expected Fed rate increase on the yuan, says \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 ' \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  group. The yuan's trading band tethers it to a fixing value within 2% in either direction against the dollar, but the dollar's relative strength has tended to push the yuan higher against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And when the Fed raises rates, the dollar will likely strengthen even more, potentially pulling the yuan up with it. "In that environment, it certainly makes sense for China's policy makers to buy some flexibility ahead of Fed lift-off, in particular since the fix had become very 'peg-like' in its stability in recent months," Goldman says. "In short, this is about Fed lift-off most obviously and further dollar strength." (james.ramage@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 13:06 EDT - The yuan's devaluation will hurt American steelmakers, says the industry's chief Washington lobbyist. "\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consistently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to control the value of the yuan versus the US dollar to make their exports more competitive and impose new barriers to imports," contends \uc2 Tom Gibson\uc2 , head of the \uc2 American Iron and Steel Institute\uc2 . He calls for the US to impose more import tariffs: "Our government must address the massive damage that China's undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is causing to our nation's manufacturing sector, especially the steel industry." (john.miller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 13:00 EDT - The US now produces twice the propane it did five years ago. And RBN Energy says while exports of the barbecue fuel have surged, they'll soon skyrocket. "About the only thing that has been holding back even-more exports is shipping costs...but that's all about to come to an end." Many new liquid-petroleum-gas vessels have been ordered and will start hitting the market this year, notes RBN. And 2016 comes the opening of a bigger Panama Canal, allowing for any-sized Very Large Gas Carrier, making US/Asia trips cheaper and faster. (dan.molinski@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 12:52 EDT - Take-Two (TTWO) paid $105M in internal royalties last quarter, far above the year earlier's $8.2M, in the wake of the videogame maker turning positive. The expense is a form of profit-sharing TTWO has with its two developers and the company doesn't disclose how it's divvied up beyond being based on the developers' individual profitability. "It's a retention tool," CFO Lainie Goldstein tells WSJ. "It aligns them better with the overall company as well as our shareholders." Amid TTWO's 1Q results and upbeat view, shares rise 1.2% to $31.31. (sarah.needleman@wsj.com; @saraheneedleman)\par \par \uc2 12:49 EDT - The approaching presidential election, along with the constant cycle of congressional polls, is adding fuel to the political fire regarding China's yuan devaluation. Even before the move, Sen. Rob Portman (R., Ohio)--locked in a difficult re-election battle--and other key lawmakers from manufacturing states were backing legislation to crack down on alleged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation. Many members of Congress are insisting such measures be linked to the Trans-Pacific Partnership trade talks, which don't include China. Portman reiterated those calls today, saying the Obama administration's "refusal to take on China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation is enabling Chinese workers to have an unfair advantage over Ohio workers." Japan and other countries in the TPP oppose putting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules in the pact. (william.mauldin@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 12:45 EDT - The yuan devaluation could have a big impact on \uc2 Coca-Cola\uc2  (KO), which generates about 8% of its volumes and profit from China and has been leaning on the country for growth as soda sales slump in many other parts of the world. KO also generates about 80% of its profit outside the U.S., further exposing the company if Tuesday's move pulls down other foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the already strong dollar. KO already estimated last month that foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rates would have negative impacts of 6 percentage points on its revenue and 11 percentage points on its operating profit this year. KO slips 0.4% to $41.53. (mike.esterl@wsj.com @mikeesterl)\par \par \uc2 12:45 EDT - \uc2 Humana\uc2  (HUM) and \uc2 Aetna\uc2 's (AET) joint proxy statement for their planned merger includes new details about the dance among the biggest health insurers, which were talking to one another as early as last year about possible deals. Things ended with HUM pairing with AET and \uc2 Cigna\uc2  (CI) going with Anthem (ANTM). But a company referred to as "Party A," which Leerink says appears to be \uc2 UnitedHealth\uc2  (UNH), approached AET as early as last August and ultimately offered $104/share. The board concluded in January that wasn't not enough as the deal faced "significant regulatory and other risks." It also turned back a June overture from UNH which included "a significant market-based premium," partly because of continued risk concerns. AET is currently at $118. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 12:32 EDT - National oil company \uc2 Petroleos Mexicanos\uc2  and its oil workers union are facing a midnight deadline in contract talks that are critical for the firm's survival in an energy market that was opened up to private companies last year. A key sticking point for the 2015-2017 contract is pension benefits. \uc2 Pemex\uc2  has $99B in pension liabilities and the federal government has agreed to assume a large chunk of that based on future pension savings. \uc2 Pemex\uc2  wants to increase the retirement age to 65 from 55 and move toward a pension savings fund with contributions by the firm and its workers. \uc2 Pemex\uc2  and the union often reach last-minute contract deals, but this time the stakes are high. \uc2 Pemex\uc2  faces low oil prices, declining production and $84B in debt that is making some investors nervous, analysts say. (laurence.iliff@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 12:26 EDT - The dollar is stronger against most rivals and emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of China's unexpected move to set its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have gotten dragged down alongside the yuan as the yen, New Zealand kiwi and Aussie dollar all lose ground against the greenback; it's up 0.3% at Y125. The euro gets bid as well, even rising against the dollar, gaining 0.2% to $1.1039. Commonwealth \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  says the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is benefiting from an unwind of trades which sold the euro against better-yielding investments in China. (cynthia.lin@wsj.com; @cynthialin_dj)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 11, 2015 13:37 ET (17:37 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150811eb8b002ob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
