\par\par \b \uc2 Nikkei Down 0.7% Midday as Asian Bourses Fall -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2015\par 05:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0313 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Nikkei is down 0.7% at 20394.41 midday extending its early losses, now on pace for its 3rd loss in the last 4 sessions. All other major Asian bourses are also lower. "There is still plenty of regional sensitivity to negative equity sentiment--especially regarding Chinese equities and their volatility," says an equity trading director at a European brokerage. "Worries that corporate earnings may disappoint just adds to the case for taking money off the table for a lot of investors." Recently bid up drug makers are leading the market lower, with \uc2 Shionogi & Co\uc2 . (4507.TO) down 2.3% at Y5,040 and Eisai (4523.TO) down 3.5% at Y8,138. (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0310 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] A federal judge last week dismissed a lawsuit against \uc2 AXA\uc2 's U.S. unit involving controversial "captive" insurance. Captives are affiliated entities that hold some claims and aren't subject to the same strict funding requirements that insurers are when holding obligations directly. The suit was brought by policy holders who alleged \uc2 AXA\uc2  made "materially misleading representations as to its financial condition" by failing to disclose transaction details. The judge said "the pervasiveness of shadow insurance in New York... may well pose a threat to the stability and reliability of the state's insurance system" but plaintiffs didn't establish injury. \uc2 AXA\uc2  said these are "perfectly legal transactions that [New York Department of Financial Services] vetted and approved." (leslie.scism@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0256 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/JPY weakens, briefly touching 123.49, its lowest since July 15, as stock market weakness prompts investors' flight into the perceived safety of the JPY, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Securities\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Kenji Yoshii. "The yen is being bought as stocks remain weak," he says. The Nikkei is down 0.7% midday. Investors are already taking a wait-and-see stance ahead of key events such as the FOMC and the release of U.S. GDP data later this week, he says. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0248 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The bullish USD/INR technical chart suggests that more U.S. dollar strength - thereby rupee weakness - is likely in the near term. The pair is above the Ichimoku Cloud consolidation zone - which has now turned into a support level at 63.87 - and is also inside the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel that points to an interim ceiling of 64.56. But rupee weakness may be mitigated by the continued decline of crude oil prices. U.S. oil production remains near multi-decade highs, even as drillers fret over the impending influx of Iranian oil into the global supply chain. Cheaper imported fuel costs will keep India's current account deficit more manageable, which would thus improve the economic fundamentals that might encourage more foreign investors to place their bets on India. USD/INR is expected to open at 64.07 from its Friday close of 64.10. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0247 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] EUR/GBP Intraday: Upside prevails. The pair stays above its key support at 0.7040 and remains on the upside. The intraday relative strength index lacks downward momentum. Thus, even though a continuation of the consolidation cannot be ruled out, its extent should be limited. A first upside target is set at July 23 top at 0.7100. A break above this resistance would open the way to further bounce towards 0.7130 and 0.7150 in extension. Only a break below the key support at 0.7040 would call for further consolidation towards 0.7010 at first and towards July 23 bottom at 0.6985 in extension. This content was produced exclusively for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  by Trading Central (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ), a leading investment research and commentary service specializing in technical analysis. (kenneth.howe@wsj.com) () \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0244 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China is very likely to further widen the yuan's trading band from currently 2% to 3% in two months' time, say CICC analysts. The estimate came after China's State Council last week said it would further expand the trading band in a policy to support the nation's exports and imports sectors. The move to give the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more leeway to trade will help Beijing's efforts to lobby the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  to include the yuan in its basket of global reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at a scheduled review late this year, CICC analysts say. After the yuan's trading band widening, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may weaken against U.S. dollar in a short run, the analysts predict. But the move could help \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gradually exit from market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , they add. (grace.zhu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0236 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] A support base at 135.45 has formed for EUR/JPY and has allowed for a temporary stabilisation. The pair is taking a breather and is moving sideways. However, as long as the support base at 135.45 is not broken down, further upside is expected with the next resistances set at July 23 top at 136.45 and then at 136.85 in extension. A break above these levels would call for further advance towards 137.30 as possible. Only a break below the key support at 135.45 would open the way to further weakness towards July 22 bottom at 134.95 and then to July 21 bottom at 134.45 as likely. This content was produced exclusively for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  by Trading Central (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ), a leading investment research and commentary service specializing in technical analysis. (kenneth.howe@wsj.com)() \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0233 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/CAD pair stays above its key support at 1.3010 and remains on the upside. The 20-period moving average is still above its 50-period one, while the intraday relative strength index is around 50 and lacks downward momentum. Thus, even though a continuation of the consolidation cannot be ruled out, its extent should be limited. Further upside is expected with the next horizontal resistances and overlaps set at 1.3070 and then at July 24 top at 1.3095 in extension. A break above these levels would call for further advance towards 1.3125 as possible. Only a break below the horizontal support at 1.3010 would open the way to further weakness towards 1.2980 at first. A second alternative target is set at July 23 bottom at 1.295 as possible. This content was produced exclusively for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  by Trading Central (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ), a leading investment research and commentary service specializing in technical analysis. (kenneth.howe@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0230 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/CHF pair has clearly reversed up, supported by the rising 20- and 50-period moving averages. A strong support base around 0.9585 has formed, which should limit any downside room. Besides, the oscillator RSI is above its neutrality area at 50%, and calls for a new bounce. As long as 0.9585 holds on the downside, the pair is expected to post a new recovery to challenge 0.9650 (July 21's top) at first, if breakout, look for further advance to 0.9680. Alternatively, below 0.9585 look for further downside with 0.9555 & 0.9535 as targets.This content was produced exclusively for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  by Trading Central (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ), a leading investment research and commentary service specializing in technical analysis. (kenneth.howe@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0222 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The GBP/USD pair seems to be stuck under its horizontal level at 1.5535, which was recently confirmed as a major resistance. In terms of technical indicators, the momentum indicator relative strength index is mixed with a bearish bias. The trending indicators, such as the key moving averages call for an intraday technical rebound, but the upward potential is likely to be limited by the resistance at 1.5535. To sum up, as long as 1.5535 holds on the upside, look for 1.5465 & 1.5445 in extension. Alternatively, only the upside breakout of 1.5535 would trigger further upside with 1.5570 & 1.5610 as targets. This content was produced exclusively for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  by Trading Central (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2  ), a leading investment research and commentary service specializing in technical analysis. (kenneth.howe@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0218 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Crude oil futures are slightly higher in Asian trade with traders buying to take advantage of a fall in prices last week. The trading sentiment is still weak with supplies from Iran expected to add to a supply overhang, which has kept crude oil under pressure. Nymex oil futures are up 3 cents at $48.03/bbl, Brent crude is up 15 cents at $54.60/bbl. (biman.mukherji@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0208 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The NZD/USD pair remains weak below its key resistance at 0.6625, and seems likely to re-test its nearest support at 0.6555. The risk of the downside breakout of this threshold is still high, as the intraday relative strength index lacks upward momentum, and the declining 50-period simple moving average acts as a resistance role. In these perspectives, a break below 0.6555 would trigger a drop towards 0.653, and even to 0.6500 as possible. Alternatively, above 0.6625, look for further upside with 0.6655 & 0.6695 as targets. This content was produced exclusively for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  by Trading Central (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ), a leading investment research and commentary service specializing in technical analysis. (kenneth.howe@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 26, 2015 23:14 ET (03:14 