\par\par \b \uc2 State-Backed CSFC Punts on Some Highly Speculative Stocks -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2015\par 09:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0757 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] What state-backed \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Securities\uc2  Finance Corp bought exactly during its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a mystery, but it's now known to have acquired some highly speculative stocks. According to replies from listed firms on "Interaction Easy" of the Shenzhen exchange, an online platform that allows firms to communicate directly--and publicly--with investors, CSFC is among the top shareholders of \uc2 Fujian Cosunter Pharmaceutical\uc2  (300436.CN) and Navinfo (002405.CN). CSFC holds a 4.63% of Cosunter, making it the second largest shareholder of the pharmaceutical company. Cosunter was listed on Shenzhen's ChiNext board in April and its stock has jumped fourteen-fold since its debut. It is trading at 110 times earnings and 60 times its book value, even after losing 40% of its value from its peak. According to Navinfo, CSFC is the third biggest shareholder of the firm.\par \par \uc2  The Tencent-backed (0700.HK) digital map provider is trading at a price-earnings ratio of 160, and about 11 times its book value. (jacky.wong@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @jackycwong) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0744 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Spot gold inched up in late Asia trade but was still trading below the psychological threshold of $1,100/oz. Physical demand from China and India, the two largest consumers, have picked up since prices fell to a five-year low earlier this week. But the expectations of a rise in interest rates has dampened a price recovery. Spot gold is trading at $1,097.38/oz, up from the opening price of $1,094.51/oz. (biman.mukherji@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0742 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Spain's 2Q job creation was nothing short of surprising, says Raj Badiani, an analyst with \f28 \uc2 \f2 IHS\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Total jobs in the economy expanded by 3% Y/Y, or 513,500, the strongest such increase since the latter stages of the peak property boom year of 2007; the numbers slightly surpassed expectations, he adds, noting that 2014 as a whole saw a 1.2% increase in total jobs; "our current employment projections of gains of 2.7% in 2015 and 2.1% in 2016 now appear to be pessimistic." Mr. Badiani reckons "the avalanche of new jobs" should help to ease PM Rajoy's pre-election jitters after poor results in May regional and municipal elections. (david.roman@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0741 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Hungary is likely to keep interest rates on hold "as long as possible," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It forecasts Hungary will keep rates unchanged until at least 4Q 2016 and raise them "only very gradually" thereafter. A hawkish shift in FOMC policy outlook and/or a deterioration in Hungary's strong current account surplus could force Hungary to raise rates earlier, Citi says. Given that mortgages, following their conversion from a foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , are benchmarked to the 3-month Budapest Interbank Offered Rate, or Bubor, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate increases may become a politically sensitive issue ahead of Hungary's next parliamentary elections, due in spring 2018, says Citi economist Eszter Gargyan. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0722 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/SGD rose further Thursday, implying a weaker Singapore dollar versus the greenback, despite consumer price data coming in line with forecasts, reducing the likelihood of further monetary policy easing. Data released Thursday showed inflation fell for an eighth consecutive month to match economists' median expectation of -0.3%. In May, the headline CPI declined 0.4%. Core CPI, which excludes accommodation costs and private road transport costs, and is the key indicator that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  monitors in deciding on policy, inched higher to 0.2% from 0.1%. The Singapore dollar ought to have recouped on lowered odds for a MAS adjustment of the Singapore dollar's value at its next meeting in October, but the overriding strength of the U.S. dollar due to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  rate-increase expectations continues to drive USD/SGD higher. USD/SGD is now 1.3677 from its Wednesday close of 1.3651. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0719 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Deloitte's decision to resign as auditor of troubled Sound Global (0967.HK) is a sign of the "angst" it's gone through, says Trung Nguyen, analyst at Lucror Analytics. Sound Global wasn't doing enough to address Deloitte's "audit issues", according to an exchange filing. Short-seller Emerson Analytics identified a 2 billion yuan shortfall in the firm's books in February. The firm has since lost two independent directors, including the head of its audit committee, and it has yet to file its 2014 financial report. Sound Global plans to hire the boutique auditing firm HLB Hodgson Impey Cheng in Deloitte's place. Nguyen says this reminds him of China Solar Energy in 2011, which also saw Deloitte resign as auditor due to a "fee" issue. HLB came in, and gave China Solar Energy a clean audit. Two years later, Chinese authorities detained three of its executives on claims of fraud. (Dominique.fong@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0719 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Spain's 2Q unemployment rate fell at a significant pace, to 22.4% from 23.8% in 1Q, as the economy added 411,000 jobs in the quarter, amid accelerating economic growth ahead of the job-intensive summer tourism season. The rate is now the lowest since 3Q '11. Even though 2Q is traditionally the best quarter for Spain's jobs market and the country still has the second-highest EU unemployment rate after Greece--at 25.6% of the workforce--the speed of Spanish improvement is remarkable: the drop of 1.4 percentage points between the 1Q and 2Q has only been matched once since the start of comparable records in 2002: last year, when the rate fell to 24.5% from 25.9%. (david.roman@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0707 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Hungary may face a need to cut its benchmark interest rate further despite its pledge to keep the key rate unchanged at its current, record low 1.35% level "for a very long time," says RBS. Further forint appreciation could be on the cards in the near term, and a sharp move lower in the EUR/HUF cross to the 300-305 range is possible, says RBS economist Gabor Ambrus. Should this forint appreciation prove lasting and should oil prices move much lower--as RBS's European rates research team expects--the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may find its commitment to steady rates hard to keep, he adds. EUR/HUF is at 307.98. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0702 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Without a clear end to Thailand's worst drought in more than a decade, the country's economy might take a heavier toll than officials have estimated, according to Krungsri Securities. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  earlier projected the prolonged drought could shave off the country's 2015 gross domestic product by 0.5 percentage point, while the Ministry of Agriculture forecasts economic growth might be cut by 0.3 percentage point, attributing it to delays in crop sowing in the agricultural sector. But if the drought continues, it could cause seawater to flow upstream and affect the industrial sector, Krungsri says, further lowering Thailand's GDP. The government projected the country's economy to grow around 3.0% this year. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @nopbkk) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: FLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0701 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The summer months have typically been characterized by less supply, less volatility and a drift lower in Bund yields, say analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 . So far, this pattern is holding up, with 10-yr Bund yields lower the 0.81% level they started the month. "Event risk haven flows may be subsiding, but seasonals, upcoming month-end index extensions, the lack of supply over August and ECB QE all point to lower Bund yields over the near-term," says Citi. 10-yr Bunds quoted at 0.695%. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0654 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/KRW ended Thursday at 1,165.1, its highest since June 2012 implying that the won is at its weakest versus the U.S. dollar in three years. The main factors in play were stronger-than-expected U.S. existing home sales data, as well as below-forecast data on South Korea 2Q gross domestic product. The economy grew by 0.3% on-quarter, versus a median expectation for 0.4%. The negative impact of the MERS virus outbreak on tourism was part of the reason for the slowdown. Looking ahead, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  may consider another interest rate cut to buffer against further economic weakness, and this may be driving USD/KRW higher. When the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cuts interest rates, its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  typically depreciates due to its lower yield-earning potential. USD/KRW close compares with 1,153.6 on Wednesday, implying a 1% depreciation of the won against the greenback. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0646 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--EUR/CHF has been moving higher over the past week, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and is now testing pivotal resistance at 1.05. Says a sustained break above here will target the 1.06 area, while failure will see bearish pressure return for a move back to the recent 1.0342 and 1.0280 lows. Now at 1.0490. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 23, 2015 03:57 ET (07:57 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150723eb7n0018u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
