\par\par \b \uc2 Stock Moves Might Not Taint Yuan's Image Yet -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2015\par 18:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 12:08 EDT - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the country's stock-market rout has come as the government is ramping up its campaign to get the yuan into the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's SDR basket later this year. Doing so would be a big step in making the yuan a global reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Marc Chandler at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  says the heavy-handed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not have "much bearing on the factors that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  looks at to decide." He says the first one--the role of exports--isn't a problem. Second, the yuan has to be freely accessible, which Chandler deems "a judgment call." He adds China would have to adopt the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's best practices, which includes publishing reserves' composition. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 11:29 EDT - Greece's bailout deal is far from secured. Putting aside bailout fatigue and a host of other mountainous hurdles the tentative deal faces, the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's dour assessment of Greece's debt-relief needs bolsters German Finance Minister Wolfgang Schauble's argument that a Greek exit may be the better alternative. Given Schauble's strong approval ratings--by some measures surpassing Chancellor \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2 --don't rule out Germany's political process forcing a Grexit ahead. (ian.talley@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 11:25 EDT - For Fitch, creditworthiness among emerging nations has generally deteriorated this year, with downgrades outnumbering upgrades by a more-than 4-1 rate. The ratings firm notes oil's slump led to 4 cuts, making it the "most-important current sovereign-rating driver." Fitch sees Brent averaging $65/barrel for the year, but a failure to recover would likely result in more downgrades. And while the firm doesn't expect a Fed rate hike to trigger widespread issues across emerging markets, tighter US policy risks exacerbating financing pressure among those with large current-account deficits and debt burdens. (cynthia.lin@wsj.com; @cynthialin_dj)\par \par \uc2 11:24 EDT - \uc2 Barclays\uc2  upgraded soft-drink bottler \uc2 Coca-Cola Femsa\uc2  (KOF) to overweight from equal weight, citing its marketing and sales strategies now that the worst risks -- devaluation in Venezuela and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness elsewhere, as well as soda taxes in Mexico -- "have already materialized, and have in fact showcased KOF's strength." KOF recently up 0.6% at $80.97, versus Barclay's $92 price target. (anthony.harrup@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 10:37 EST -- Colombia's flagship airline \uc2 Avianca Holdings\uc2  (AVH) yesterday announced a deal to sell 30% of its Lifemiles customer loyalty program to US-based private equity firm \uc2 Advent International\uc2  -- a stake valued at $343.7M. The deal will help the airline pay down debt and buy new planes. Moreover, the deal will offset the $270M to $280M the company has trapped in Venezuela due to that country's capital controls. "With all this in mind, added to the company's recovery in financial results supported by the deep decrease in oil prices and management operating efficiencies, we keep \uc2 Avianca Holdings\uc2  as one of our top picks," note Bancolombia analysts. Shares rose 4% to $10.78 in New York on Monday. (sara.munoz@wsj.com; @sarasmunoz)\par \par \uc2 10:35 EDT - Gol's (GOL, GOLL4.BR) $446M capitalization plan comes at an important moment for the Brazilian airline to guarantee its financial flexibility as the company faces cost pressures and a drop in demand, says \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Investors Services. The carrier is selling a combined $146M of stock to its controlling shareholder and Delta (\uc2 DAL\uc2 ), while also planning to borrow another $300M, guaranteed by Delta. "In addition to enforcing the companies' partnership, we expect that the guarantee of Delta will lower the interest rate on the notes that Gol would otherwise obtain absent the guarantee," \uc2 Moody's\uc2  says, noting it considers the capitalization plan as positive for Gol's creditworthiness. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1413 GMT Germans appear to be backing Chancellor \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2 's Greek policy despite distrust toward the Greek government, according to an opinion poll published Tuesday. Ms. Merkel has done a good job in helping to achieve eurozone leaders' latest bailout deal say 55% of the 1,001 people polled by Forsa institute for Stern and RTL while 31% said it would have been better to force Greece out of the eurozone. Eight out of ten, however, have doubts the Greek government will implement the agreed reform measures, with only 14% saying they trust Athens will do as promised. Eurozone leaders have agreed Greece could get up to EUR86 billion in fresh loans as long as Athens enacts several bills by Wednesday, such as pension reforms and higher taxes. (andrea.thomas@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10:12 EDT - Brazil's lousy May retail sales, which fell a greater-than-expected 0.9% from the previous month, point to more tough times ahead for the nation's merchants, according to Barclay's. Brazil's unemployment is rising, real disposable income is falling and credit is tight. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' projects household consumption in Brazil will contract 1.2% this year. "We do not expect a recovery in retail sales anytime soon," the bank said. (marla.dickerson@wsj.com; @medWSJ)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1405 GMT Monday's agreement with Greece "seems to be more about France and Germany staying friendly than solving the Greek problem," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russell Investments\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' senior investment strategist Wouter Sturkenboom. The strategist reckons that slippage in terms of reforms and privatization--to be implemented by Greece--is "almost guaranteed", and so is disappointment with respect to Greek economic performance. "The Greek issue will not go away but continue to haunt the eurozone for years to come with the review cycle as a drumbeat of bad news," Mr. Sturkenboom says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10:04 EDT - Technology has helped to broaden participation in the $5T/day trading of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, but it comes at serious costs if traders don't adhere to best practices, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  markets chief Simon Potter. Pointing to investigations which last year revealed broad misconduct and collusion in the spot market, he warns the public stands to lose if faith in the global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market crumbles. "In the absence of a single centralized and comprehensive global regulator of this highly global market, collaborative efforts between the private and official sectors play an important role." (cynthia.lin@wsj.com; @cynthialin_dj)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10:00 EDT -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Peru's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could leave behind its neutral bias and move towards a more-restrictive monetary policy should inflationary pressures increase, says Scotiabank. "The increase in inflationary expectations and the persistence of pressure from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market shifts upwards the bias" on where policy goes. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has stood pat since January. June's CPI was 3.5%, above the bank's 1-3% target range. (robert.kozak@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1353 GMT History shows that crises lead to more union, not less, says Thushka Maharaj, global strategist for multi-asset solutions at \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Asset Management\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Some good can come out of this crisis if European authorities seize this opportunity to deepen fiscal and structural foundations and speed up the move towards 'ever closer' union," the strategist says. Specifically, concrete steps on completing the banking union and a pan-European guarantee scheme would be supportive for risk assets, particularly peripheral sovereign spreads, she says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 14, 2015 12:08 ET (16:08 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150714eb7e002dp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
