\par\par \b \uc2 Nikkei up at Midday--Fate of Greece Keeps Market on Edge -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2015\par 05:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0307 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Nikkei is +0.4% at 19937 midday, recovering from a modestly negative start. "Thanks to a rebound in China shares--where the composite Shanghai SSE index is up 5.7%--Japan stocks are seeing a decent amount of buying support, but the selloff in \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  (9983.TO) is a big drag due to its huge weight in the Nikkei," says an equity trading director at a foreign brokerage. "In terms of short-term volatility, China continues to exert strong influence, but Sunday will tell more about the mid-term picture, especially if Greece ends up leaving the eurozone. Meanwhile, U.S. earnings reports will influence Japan individual stock and sector movements." \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  remains down 6.1% at 53,930 yen. (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0306 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The price gap between different quality iron ore narrowed as the closely followed 62% price plummeted to decade lows, but \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2  doesn't expect that to last for too long. In recent weeks, the spread between the 62% and 58% ores has narrowed to 13%, which reflects the average in 2012\u8209\'20\'112013 when prices were considerably higher and compares to a record 33% last July, says analyst Vivek Dhar. "Despite the recent convergence of the two benchmarks, we expect the spread to remain wide as low iron-ore prices encourage steel mills in China towards higher-quality iron ore," Dhar says. Ore with 62% iron content rose 9.5% Thursday to US$48.30/ton, according to The Steel Index. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0305 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Lieutenant General Hernando Iriberri was appointed Philippine military chief on Friday, becoming the sixth commander to serve during the five-year-old presidency of Benigno Aquino. The Philippine military is implementing a long-overdue modernization program as it grapples with territorial disputes with China, but a rule forcing soldiers to retire at 56 is disrupting those efforts, Philippine defense analysts have long complained, as it necessitates constant reshuffles of the top brass. The outgoing commander, General Gregorio Pio Catapang, held the top post for just under a year. Iriberri himself hits retirement age in May. Aquino had pledged to introduce fixed three-year terms of armed forces chiefs, irrespective of age, but his failure to deliver on that means the Philippine military must continue to live without leadership continuity as it attempts to transform itself into a viable outfit. (trefor.moss@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0304 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Australia dollar has risen 0.7% versus the U.S. dollar as stock markets in China rebound a second day, sparking demand for the risk-sensitive commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The daily AUD/USD chart still shows a bearish bias but this could be nullified if the pair closes Friday above 0.7520 and thus out of the Bollinger downtrend channel. Confirmation that the downtrend channel has been negated could motivate short-covering that might propel AUD/USD toward the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance line at 0.7641 in the days ahead. The Shanghai composite stock index appears to have finally gained some traction, rising 6.1% Friday, after a slew of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures announced by the authorities. The latest move by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's government was to ban selling by major shareholders, and to investigate "malicious" short-selling. AUD/USD is now 0.7488 from its Thursday close of 0.7442. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0301 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] One might argue that the sharp drop in Australian home-loan approvals in May removes a major hurdle to a further interest rate cut in Australia. The 6.1% seasonally-adjusted fall from April is eye-popping, so too the 3.2% drop in investor lending over the same period. Combined, they suggest that recently applied clamps on bank lending to property investors are working and heat is coming out of the housing market. But the question of whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is feeling the need to cut rates again is also worth asking after news Thursday of lower-than-expected unemployment in June. It's likely the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  is noting a solid improvement in the job market. Certainly the RBA's forecast of a cyclical peak in unemployment of 6.5% looks set to be missed by a big margin. NAB economist Tapas Strickland said the RBA looks to be "comfortably on hold" until the end of the year. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter: @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0241 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Malaysian crude palm-oil futures are higher on gains in overnight soyoil and Dalian palm, although gains may be limited on a slightly stronger ringgit and ahead of industry data due out in the global day, say traders. A Kuala Lumpur-based trader says volatility in the Chinese market and a potential Grexit are still risk factors; he warns of long liquidation ahead of the weekend when there will be a \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  summit. Benchmark December crude palm-oil futures on the Bursa Malaysia Derivatives closed MYR35 higher at MYR2,185/ton; they were last MYR20 higher at MYR2,207/ton. (huileng.tan@wsj.com; Twitter: @huileng_tan) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0240 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Singapore Press Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  (T39.SG) is up 0.5% at S$4.07 after the media firm reports a 10% rise in net profit in its fiscal third quarter. Net profit was 98.2 million Singapore dollars in the April-to-June period, compared with S$89.6 million a year ago. Total revenue rose 0.5% to S$315 million. Revenue from company's property division rose 16.5% while revenue from its main media business fell 5.6% to S$233 million. The property division now accounts for about a fifth of total revenue. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0238 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Tocom rubber futures are higher in slow trade as traders take a breather to assess recent market volatility; price are supported by a weaken yen and gains in the broader Chinese market. Spot trade is slow, with more buyers than sellers, although few are in a hurry to lock in deals amid price swings, say traders. Benchmark December rubber trades Y1.3 higher at Y210.9/kg. (huileng.tan@wsj.com; Twitter: @huileng_tan) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0227 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Copper has bounced 7.5% from its six-year low, but still trades down 2% compared with this time a week ago. At least in some analysts' eyes, though, it is unlikely to stay down for long. "As the market risks in China and Greece are easing, the returned investment demand for cheap copper will support a strong rally in copper price, in our view," says Argonaut Securities analyst Helen Lau. LME three-month copper trades up 0.1% at US$5,634/ton. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0222 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The broad U.S. dollar retreat, on the back of an improvement in risk appetite Thursday, has dragged USD/IDR to the lower end of its 13,300-13,350 consolidation range. If the pair closes Friday inside the Bollinger downtrend channel which begins at 13,300, more dollar weakness and thereby rupiah strength can be expected in the short-term. Investor sentiment is improving after the Shanghai composite index on Thursday finally rebounded from its recent collapse; the benchmark stock index is up 3.3% so far today. Chinese authorities have gone all-out to reverse the selloff in stocks - which has affected risk appetite throughout the region and thereby boosted the safe haven U.S. dollar - but analysts are concerned that this meddling in the stock market could dent confidence in the longer run. USD/IDR is now 13,305 from its Thursday close of 13,332. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0209 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] There remains upside potential in surgical gloves-to-condoms producer Ansell (ANN.AU) from further bolt-on acquisitions, but for now \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  says, the balance tilts toward headwinds from an uncertain medium-term macroeconomic outlook, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements and some evidence of rising raw-material costs. It retains a neutral investment rating and trims its price target to A$27/share from A$29.90. ANN shares are down 0.4% at A$24.75. (robb.stewart@wsj.com; Twitter: @RobbMStewart) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0200 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Investors should consider using the recent nickel-led pullback in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Western Areas Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (WSA.AU) shares as a buying opportunity, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "WSA has quality assets backed by a strong balance sheet and disciplined management," it says. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  keeps its overweight rating and A$4.80 target on the stock, which trades up 2.3% at A$3.11/share. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; Twitter: @RhiannonHoyle) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 09, 2015 23:07 ET (03:07 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150710eb7a000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
