\par\par \b \uc2 India Shares Open Lower on Weak Regional Cues -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,630 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2015\par 06:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0402 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Indian shares open lower Wednesday tracking weakness in other regional markets. The \uc2 S&P\uc2  BSE Sensex falls 0.9% to 27,914.49, while the National Stock Exchange's Nifty index also declines 1% to 8,424.15. Among the major losers, metals and energy companies decline on fears of a demand slowdown in China, the biggest buyer of everything from iron ore and coal to copper and gold. Vedanta (500295.BY) is down 3.5%, Hindalco (500440.BY) falls 3.2%, while \uc2 Tata Steel\uc2  (500470.BY) loses 1.7%. However, pharmaceutical companies rise as they are less dependent on commodities and as investors look for safe haven stocks. (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0358 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Despite the USD/JPY's fall to 121.96 earlier in session amid a deepening risk-averse stance on the China stocks tumble, the pair is still positioned in a recent range between 121.50-124.50, says Toshihiko Sakai, senior manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial products trading division at Mitsubishi UFJ Trust and Banking. "The China stocks falloff is the biggest market mover," says Sakai. "Volatility is getting higher .... but I think (the pair is) not out of this range," he says, pointing out downside support at 121.70 (its low on Monday soon after Greece roiled the global markets after a weekend referendum).(hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor SXS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0349 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The plunge in Chinese brokers' share prices is evidence that the individual investor has lost confidence in the market, says head of research at Core Pacific-Yamaichi International Castor Pang. "The market sentiment in Hong Kong is that China's central government has been unable to stabilize the A-share market," he says. With the Chinese market having lost over 25% of its value since mid-June, broker revenues will be unable to keep up with the steady rise in the first half of 2015, which enjoyed a bull market. "Investors will be unwilling to continue holding these stocks," adds Pang. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citic Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  (6030.HK), \f28 \uc2 \f2 GF Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1776.HK), \f28 \uc2 \f2 Huatai Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  (6886.HK), \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guolian Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1456.HK), and China Galaxy Securities (6881.HK) drop by 11.75% to 15.50% in Hong Kong Wednesday. (anjie.zheng@wsj.com; Twitter: @anjiezheng) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0341 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Renewed selling of Chinese shares and a slump in commodities prices is weighing heavily on Australia's share market, with broad selling wiping out much of Tuesday's rally. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 ASX\f28 \uc2 \f2  200 is down 1.6% at 5490.6, with all industry subindexes in the red, led by mining and energy. Base metals dropped amid worries about demand after the Shanghai Composite fell again despite government efforts to stabilize the market, while iron ore continued its slide to below US$50/ton. Analysts say sentiment also has been dampened by the simmering Greek crisis. "If the last couple of weeks are a guide, traders are likely to batten down the hatches by Friday in anticipation of the increasingly familiar routine of Greek induced volatility on Monday morning," Ric Spooner, chief market analyst at CMC Markets, says. Woodside (WPL.AU) is down 2.4%, Oil Search (OSH.AU) is 2% lower and Santos (STO.AU) is 3.4% weaker. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BHP.AU) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RIO.AU) are down 2.5% and 2.4%, while fell iron-ore producer Fortescue (FMG.AU) is down 5%. The four biggest banks are down by between 1.9% and 2.5%. (robb.stewart@wsj.com; Twitter: @RobbMStewart) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0339 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/TWD rises, tracking the greenback's strength against most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on weak risk appetite, says a local trader. Sharp declines in Taiwan stocks (the Taiex is down 2.4%) due to below-view export data and falling China stocks are also weighing on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "Foreign investors are buying the U.S. dollar actively...but a few exporters are still willing to sell," the trader adds. The pair is at 31.024, higher than 30.980 traded before the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday, which lifted it to 31.162 at the close of onshore trading session, traders say. Taiwan government bonds are stronger as some investors are shifting their funds to bonds due to weak local stocks. The most-traded 10-year bond yield falls to 1.4734% versus 1.4979% late Tuesday; a bond trader says the yield is likely to test its major support at 1.4500% soon. (fanny.liu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0337 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Never mind Greece and its dire debt issues. The bigger picture is how China's $8 trillion stock market could "implode," says Netherlands-based Robeco, which manages $300 billion globally. Its chief investment officer, Lukas Daalder, says despite fears of a 2008 crash, the Chinese government will likely cushion further free-falls in a market that has lost one-third of its value since mid-June. "Given the negative spill-over effects to the broader Chinese economy, we expect the authorities to remain \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as much as possible," Daalder writes in a note to investors. "This does not mean that they will be aiming to get the stock market back up to the levels seen in mid-June, but they have a clear interest to lower the current volatility seen in the market." How long \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will wait for its next \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains to be seen. The Shanghai Composite crashes 4.5% Wednesday morning. (Dominique.fong@wsj.com; Twitter: @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0335 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The chief economist of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippines' Department of Finance\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday the government must increase tax on oil to shore up revenue collection amid lower petroleum prices and tame inflation. "This trend [for lower oil prices] may be reversed in the near future. As such, the government should take advantage of the currently lower energy prices and adjust gasoline taxes before international oil prices resume their upward trend," said Finance Undersecretary Gil Beltran. The Philippines imports around 120 million barrels oil a year. (cris.larano@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0323 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Malaysia's industrial production index likely rose 3.0% in May, according to the median forecast of 15 economists polled by The Wall Street Journal, as sluggish global demand and weak commodities prices weighed on the country's manufacturing and mining sectors. This compares with April's 4.0% year-over-year gain. The official data are due Friday 0400 GMT. "Manufacturing activities appears to be soft across the region as overall external demand remains weak," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Malaysia's exports contracted for the second consecutive month in May, down 6.7% year-on-year. Shipments of electronic products, which make up about a third of total exports, slipped 0.6% in May while exports of liquefied natural gas fell 48%. "Low global energy prices continue to drag on mining production, while the introduction of a goods and services tax last month is dampening manufacturing," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (jason.ng@wsj.com; Twitter: @ByJasonNg) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0312 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Although the impending departure of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Craig Billings\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a loss for slot-machine company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aristocrat Leisure\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ALL.AU) but the appointment of Pat Ramsey to succeed him as chief digital officer is a positive, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. It notes that Ramsey, who takes up the post in January, was formerly CEO of Multimedia Games and has held senior roles at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Caesars Entertainment\f28 \uc2 \f2  (CZR) prior to that. The brokerage maintains a buy recommendation and A$10/share target on ALL, which is down 0.7% at A$8.23. (robb.stewart@wsj.com; Twitter: @RobbMStewart) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0309 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] A contract from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Saudi Aramco\f28 \uc2 \f2  doesn't help \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ezra Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' (5DN.SG) shares, likely because the company doesn't provide financial details about the contract. Ezra is down 1.8% at S$0.161 as investors continue to sell its stock following a rights issue announcement earlier. Ezra says on Wednesday that its subsea services unit \f28 \uc2 \f2 EMAS AMC\f28 \uc2 \f2  and a unit of India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Larsen & Toubro\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500510.BY) have won a six-year contract from the Saudi state-owned oil company to provide engineering, project management and installation services for offshore facilities such as platforms, pipelines and cables. Ezra is selling shares in the rights issue at S$0.105 apiece. The Straits Times Index is down 0.8%. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0307 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] In Asia, the drop in China shares is a much bigger issue than Greece, and traders see this play out in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the Aussie dollar which has tested below US$0.7400, says Stephen Innes, senior trader at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 OANDA\f28 \uc2 \f2  Australia. "China continues to be the elephant in the room, the recent meltdown of the Chinese equity market continues to be a challenge for Greece for top billing. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter: @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0303 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Singapore Post\f28 \uc2 \f2  (S08.SG) is up 0.8% at S$1.905 after announcing that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Group Holding\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BABA) is investing another US$138.6 million in the company. Alibaba will buy 107.6 million new \f28 \uc2 \f2 Singapore Post\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares at S$1.74 per share, taking its stake to 14.51% from 10.23%. The two companies will also deepen their collaboration that began last year when Alibaba first invested in the Singapore firm. In contrast, the Straits Times Index is down 0.8%. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 08, 2015 00:02 ET (04:02 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150708eb7800094\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
