\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2015\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Nowotny: If Greece Misses Payment, Funds Will Be Cut Off \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be forced to cut off liquidity to Greece should the Mediterranean country miss its July 20 deadline to pay back the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a member of \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2 's governing council said Monday night. (published 2228 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par White House Calls on Greece to Deliver on Previous Economic Promises \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Obama administration, after pressing Greece and its European creditors to compromise for weeks, returned to its familiar role on Monday of prodding from the sidelines. (published 2159 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Saudi Arabia to Invest up to $10 Billion in Russia \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabia has signed a commitment to invest up to $10 billion in Russia, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russian Direct Investment Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 2100 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2 : Fund Chief Lagarde Discusses Greek Referendum With PM Tsipras -- Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  told Greek Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras on Monday that the emergency lender can't disburse any bailout cash until the debt-ridden country clears its arrears, according to a spokeswoman. (published 2043 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Merkel, Hollande Say Greece Needs Proposals for Brussels Meeting -- Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The leaders of Germany and France on Monday called on Greece to craft urgent proposals to prevent a catastrophic exit from the eurozone, leaving the door open to negotiations after Greek voters rebuked the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bloc in a referendum. (published 2017 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par New Greek Finance Minister Tsakalotos Thrown Into the Debt Crisis Hot Seat \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's new finance minister, Euclid Tsakalotos, will have to hit the ground running Tuesday in a race to save the country from bankruptcy and possibly crashing out of the eurozone. (published 2008 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Vanke\f28 \uc2 \f2  Plans to Issue CNY9 Billion Worth of Corporate Bonds in China \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mainland property developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Vanke Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said late Monday it plans to issue CNY9 billion worth of corporate bonds in China and will use the net proceeds to adjust its debt structure and replenish working capital. (published 0029 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Shock But Little Awe -- Heard On The Street \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (published 2211 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par China, Iran Turn Oil's World Upside Down -- Heard On The Street \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (published 2210 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Greek Bank Vortex Threatens Deal Hopes -- Heard On The Street \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (published 2206 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 6 Jul 2015 23:00 ET \par News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Premier Says First-Quarter Economic Growth Is Within Reasonable Range \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Premier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Li Keqiang\f28 \uc2 \f2  said first-half economic growth is within a reasonable range and main economic indicators have stabilized and show positive signs. (published 0119 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Watching Greece, El Nino Effects on Inflation \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A significant slow down in June inflation is unlikely to prompt the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut interest rates, even as officials watch developments in Greece and the continuing impact of El Nino on the farm sector. (published 0231 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Taiwan Consumer Prices Fall in June, Government Says No Sign of Deflation \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer prices in Taiwan continued falling in June, but the government said it sees no sign of a deflationary spiral. (published 0056 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par New Zealand 2Q Adj Net Business Confidence +7% Vs +20% In 1Q-NZIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand business confidence fell to its lowest level in nearly three years in the second quarter as the economic outlook loses lustre. (published 0128 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Vanke\f28 \uc2 \f2  Plans to Issue CNY9 Billion Worth of Corporate Bonds in China \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mainland property developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Vanke Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said late Monday it plans to issue CNY9 billion worth of corporate bonds in China and will use the net proceeds to adjust its debt structure and replenish working capital. (published 0029 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 06, 2015 23:00 ET (03:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150707eb7700044\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
