\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Rallies as Euro and Yen Sink-- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 2,044 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2015\par 02:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2006-6.2043    6.1969-6.2122 \par USD/TWD   30.630-30.720    30.550-30.880 \par USD/KRW    1,101-1,107      1,100-1,110 \par USD/SGD   1.3500-1.3550    1.3450-1.3600 \par USD/MYR   3.6340-3.6500    3.6200-3.6660 \par USD/THB    33.66-33.80      33.50-34.00 \par USD/PHP    44.69-44.81      44.57-45.00 \par USD/IDR   13,180-13,260    13,100-13,300 \par USD/INR    63.94-64.00      63.70-64.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation higher. USD/CNY may rise Wednesday - though technical boundaries nearby may limit upside - as the pair displays a return of correlation with the U.S. dollar index this week. The latter spiked overnight as the euro sank and the yen fell to an 8-year low. \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  may hence set the daily USD/CNY benchmark rate higher accordingly, from Tuesday's 6.1172. The yuan has generally been very stable in a consolidation range between the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1), but if USD/CNY manages to break above 6.2122 and thus enters the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, it might consolidate within a higher range for the near term. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has likely been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading in a stable range, as it seeks approval to make the yuan a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ; an unstable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely reduce the yuan's credibility as a store of value. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2006 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 6.1969 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.2043 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 6.2080 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2122 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--downtrend may end. A third consecutive rise of the benchmark U.S. dollar index could negate the bearish path of USD/TWD. If the pair ends the day above 30.630 the Bollinger downtrend channel will be nullified, and short-term speculators could be spurred to trim short-USD positions. Speculative sentiment for USD/TWD - gauged by the offshore market - is turning bullish as the price of the 1-month nondeliverable forward contract creeps up toward par with that of the spot contract; it was priced at a discount earlier this week. External factors such as the ongoing Greece negotiations with Eurogroup ministers for the release of financial bailout funds continue to influence USD/Asia in general, though to a slightly less extent for USD/TWD. Recent hints from U.S. Federal Reserve chairwoman \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  that an interest rate hike is coming this year may fuel USD/TWD higher as well. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at then at 30.630 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.550 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.720 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 30.790 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.880 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--uptrend. USD/KRW gaps higher Wednesday in reciprocation of the sharp USD/JPY rally overnight which saw the Japanese yen fall to an 8-year low. The pair are closely-correlated due to \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2 's vigilance in keeping the won relatively weak versus the yen - to maintain exporters' price-competitiveness. If USD/KRW ends the day above the 1,110 top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, more upside for the pair is highly likely. The U.S. dollar index is at its strongest in a month as the euro continues to languish on Greece debt default concerns, while the U.S. Federal Reserve appears more likely to raise interest rates this year. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,101 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 1,100 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,096 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is 1,107 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,110 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 1,120 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--uptrend. USD/SGD is building on the bullish bias established Monday and may keep climbing until it hits the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that looms at around 1.3600. The daily Bollinger uptrend channel which supports the pair at 1.3405 ought to keep the pair on an upward trajectory, helped by the U.S. dollar index rallying a third session overnight as the euro sank lower on Greece default fears and the yen hit an 8-year low. The Singapore dollar has weakened significantly versus the greenback this week after Monday's disappointing inflation data which showed a sixth straight month of deflation, which might nudge the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward more monetary policy easing. But that possibility has been slightly reduced after first-quarter Gross Domestic Product growth released Tuesday came in better than earlier estimates. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.3500 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.3450 (psychological support), before 1.3405 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is 1.3550 (psychological resistance), then at 1.3600 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.3625 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--uptrend. USD/MYR is inching higher and into the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone as the U.S. dollar index rallied a third session on euro and yen weakness. The USD/MYR pair is likely to consolidate higher within the Cloud resistance zone that spans 3.6340-3.6660. But if it closes Wednesday below the Cloud, it might be a sign that upward momentum is weak and this could motivate U.S. dollar selling that might spark a downward reversal in USD/MYR. The safe haven U.S. dollar is broadly stronger as markets fear the worst-case scenario for Greece as it tries to negotiate with the Eurogroup for its bailout funds to be released - before its debt payment deadline approaches early June. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.6340 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 3.6200 (psychological support), before 3.6140 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.6500 (psychological resistance), then at 3.6660 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 3.6800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--uptrend. USD/THB has confirmed a bullish chart bias that could drive the pair toward the round-figure trading barrier of 34.00 in the near term. The pair has been tracking the U.S. dollar index - which rallied a third session overnight to a 1-month high - and is now supported by the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 33.66. Fundamentally, USD/THB ought to rise in the medium term because of the dovish rhetoric of the Thai government on interest rates juxtaposed with the increasing likelihood that the U.S. Federal Reserve will raise interest rates this year. Thai authorities have said that a cheaper baht is beneficial for its exporters, and have eased investment outflow restrictions so as to encourage baht weakness. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 33.66 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 33.50 (psychological support), before 33.47 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 33.80 (psychological resistance), then at 33.85 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 34.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--uptrend. USD/PHP is likely to keep rising toward 44.81 after the bullish technical signal of the Bollinger uptrend channel was confirmed Tuesday. The overnight surge of the U.S. dollar index - triggered by the euro and yen falling sharply - ought to power USD/PHP higher again Wednesday. USD/PHP is now above the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone, above the 200-day moving average line, and also inside the Bollinger uptrend channel - three positive chart signals. The main driver for USD/PHP continues to be external factors, lacking domestic cues. Analysts are broadly positive on the Philippine economy - though highlighting that China's growth slowdown is a mitigating factor - and don't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust monetary policy anytime soon. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.69 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 44.57 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 44.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.81 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 44.88 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--uptrend. USD/IDR may soon notch a new 17-year high as it rises along the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, powered by yet another rise of the U.S. dollar index. The safe haven dollar rallied overnight, most prominently against the beleaguered euro and the Japanese yen. USD/IDR will notch a new 17-year high if it surpasses March's peak of 13,245 but may be capped on an intraday basis by the 13,260 top of the Bollinger uptrend channel. The ongoing Greek debt negotiations will likely continue to keep the euro depressed, thereby pressuring most USD/Asia pairs higher; but if Greece manages to get bailout funds released by the Eurogroup soon, EUR/USD might rebound very sharply. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 13,180 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 13,100 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 13,000 (round figure trading barrier and daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 13,260 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 13,300 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 13,500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 26 May 2015 20:53 ET  USD/Asia Rallies as Euro and Yen Sink-- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--uptrend. USD/INR has broken out of its technical consolidation zone and entered the Bollinger uptrend channel, increasing the likelihood that the India rupee will weaken versus the U.S. dollar in the days ahead. The pair spiked late Tuesday as the U.S. dollar index surged on euro and yen weakness. The continued overnight rise of the U.S. dollar index may spur more USD/INR buying Wednesday - which would affirm the Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports at 63.94. A Wednesday close above the round-figure trading barrier of 64.00 would augment the bullish-USD sentiment. While most traders are still focused on EUR/USD fluctuations for short-term trading cues, medium-to-long term investors are looking ahead to the June 3 monetary policy meeting of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  - analysts think there is chance for an interest rate cut that would boost stocks and thereby rally the rupee. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 63.94 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 63.70 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 63.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 64.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 64.18 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 64.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 26, 2015 20:53 ET (00:53 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150527eb5r0006k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
