\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Up as Euro Tracks Lower -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 2,045 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2015\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2000-6.2043    6.1949-6.2122 \par USD/TWD   30.500-30.630    30.380-30.720 \par USD/KRW    1,094-1,100      1,090-1,110 \par USD/SGD   1.3400-1.3432    1.3376-1.3500 \par USD/MYR   3.6070-3.6270    3.6000-3.6340 \par USD/THB    33.42-33.63      33.21-33.80 \par USD/PHP    44.54-44.68      44.50-44.81 \par USD/IDR   13,170-13,250    13,090-13,300 \par USD/INR    63.43-63.65      63.20-63.88 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. USD/CNY rebounded Monday to nullify the bearish chart signal of the Bollinger downtrend channel, and is now likely to hover in a range of 6.1992-6.2103. The yuan has been very stable despite fluctuations in the U.S. dollar index - which in the past has held a stronger sway over USD/CNY. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has likely been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading in a stable range, as it seeks approval to make the yuan a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ; an unstable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely reduce the yuan's credibility as a store of value. Chinese stocks rose to a 7-year high Monday as the government announced cuts in import taxes to boost domestic consumption - part of the bigger plan to shift the manufacturing-based economy toward a consumption-driven one. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 6.1992 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1949 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1800 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2043 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 6.2103 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2122 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--downtrend. USD/TWD displays a bearish bias, capped by the 30.630 ceiling of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. The Taiwan dollar is likely to keep gaining versus the U.S. dollar, the daily chart suggests. Speculative sentiment for USD/TWD - gauged by the offshore market - is turning bearish as the price of the 1-month nondeliverable forward contract remains below that of the spot contract; it was priced at a premium late last week. If this bearish bias persists, USD/TWD may soon find the 30.000 round-figure trading barrier - a level last traded in September. External factors may come into play again as traders watch ongoing Greece negotiations with Eurogroup ministers over a restructuring of its budget. If the talks fail and bailout funds for Greece are withheld, debts repayments due to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  in June will likely be missed and markets might brace for a Greek exit from the eurozone - which would send the safe haven U.S. dollar higher. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.500 (psychological support), then at 30.380 (base of weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), before 30.200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.630 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.720 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 30.800 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation within uptrend. The recent rally of the benchmark ICE U.S. dollar index is keeping USD/KRW propped up inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. If USD/KRW ends Tuesday above 1,094 the bullish chart signal will remain in effect and could keep the South Korean won weak versus the greenback in the near term. However, the pair needs to overcome strong technical resistance at 1,101-1,110 - where the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone caps - before the dollar can rally much higher. Stocks on the benchmark KOSPI exchange might get a boost from the improvement in consumer sentiment seen Tuesday; the index rose to 105 in May versus 104 in April. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,094 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,090 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,085 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is 1,100 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,101 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 1,103 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,110 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--uptrend. The Singapore dollar weakened versus the greenback after Monday's disappointing inflation data which showed a sixth straight month of deflation, raising the possibility of further policy easing by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2 . The weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  affirmed the USD/SGD Bollinger uptrend channel which now supports the pair at a higher level of 1.3376, increasing the odds that the Singapore dollar will keep depreciating. Singapore's economy expanded 2.4% on-year in the first quarter, better than the previous forecast for 2.1% growth, data released Tuesday showed. The Singapore dollar barely reacted to the data. Traders are likely focused instead on EUR/USD, which continues to flounder - thus boosting the U.S. dollar - due to Greek debt default concerns. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.3400 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.3376 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.3350 (psychological support), before 1.3306 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is 1.3432 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.3450 (psychological resistance), before 1.3500 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--uptrend. USD/MYR now has a bullish technical stance, with Monday's confirmation of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports the pair at 3.6070. The overnight buoyancy of the U.S. dollar index - as the euro continues to linger at 1-month lows - is likely to lift USD/MYR higher Tuesday. The growing anxiety that Greece may leave the eurozone has been weighing on the euro. Greece is still struggling to negotiate the release of bailout funds from the Eurogroup - lacking which it won't be able to make debt repayments to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  due in June. If EUR/USD collapses through a key technical support level where it currently rests, the U.S. dollar might spike against the ringgit and other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.6070 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.6000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 3.5890 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.6270 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.6340 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 3.6500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--possible uptrend. USD/THB may activate a bullish chart bias if it ends Tuesday above 33.63 and thereby inside the Bollinger uptrend channel. While the overnight rise of the benchmark ICE U.S. dollar index has given the pair a mild boost, a supportive tone in EUR/USD may crimp further gains for the dollar index and thus cap USD/THB. Fundamentally, USD/THB ought to rise in the medium term because of the dovish rhetoric of the Thai government on interest rates juxtaposed with the likelihood that the U.S. Federal Reserve will raise interest rates this year. Thai authorities have said that a cheaper baht is beneficial for its exporters, and have eased investment outflow restrictions so as to encourage baht weakness. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 33.42 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 33.21 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 33.00 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 33.63 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 33.80 (psychological resistance), before 33.85 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation higher. USD/PHP may rally again on the back of the overnight rise of the U.S. dollar index and pop into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 44.68. A Tuesday close above this mark would confirm a bullish chart signal that might lead to more peso weakness versus the U.S. dollar. The main driver for the greenback continues to be the euro, which has a strong effect on the U.S. dollar index. The euro has recently been under pressure due to the possibility of Greek budget restructuring talks failing, which would mean that bailout funds will be withheld and Greece will miss its debt repayments in June. The EUR/USD pair is now testing a key technical support which if breached might trigger more selling and thereby more U.S. dollar strength. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.54 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 44.50 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone), before 44.44 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.68 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 44.81 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--uptrend. USD/IDR has engaged the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, setting it on a path higher - implying more rupiah weakness versus the U.S. dollar to come. The overnight rise of the U.S. dollar index to a 1-month high could provide a catalyst for the pair to rally again Tuesday. USD/IDR will notch a new 17-year high if it surpasses March's peak of 13,245. The main driver for U.S. dollar strength continues to be the sliding euro. Greek debt default concerns continue to drag on the euro, thus boosting the U.S. dollar index. If the EUR/USD pair dives below its current technical support level where it now bobs, USD/IDR could easily make new multi-year highs. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 13,170 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 13,090 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 13,000 (round figure trading barrier and daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 13,250 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 13,300 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 13,500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 25 May 2015 21:00 ET  USD/Asia Up as Euro Tracks Lower -- Asia Daily -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation higher. USD/INR has been in a technical consolidation zone for the past week, and may continue to meander in a range of 63.43-63.88 unless it responds to overnight U.S. dollar index strength. The pair has recently been immune to gyrations of the U.S. dollar index but if EUR/USD breaks a key technical support at which it now rests, other USD/Asia pairs are likely to react vigorously and USD/INR might be pulled higher by proxy. Fresh euro weakness may be triggered by developments in the Eurozone-Greece negotiations. But as June approaches, investors will be more focused on the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's monetary policy meeting - analysts think there is chance for an interest rate cut that would boost stocks and thereby rally the rupee. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 63.43 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 63.20 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 63.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 63.65 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 63.88 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 64.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 25, 2015 21:00 ET (01:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150526eb5q00016\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
