\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Bullish Before Greek Debt Meeting -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 2,280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2015\par 02:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2000-6.2047    6.1934-6.2133 \par USD/TWD   30.650-30.800    30.500-30.940 \par USD/KRW    1,093-1,100      1,090-1,107 \par USD/SGD   1.3345-1.3400    1.3300-1.3450 \par USD/MYR   3.6040-3.6340    3.6000-3.6500 \par USD/THB    33.50-33.65      33.29-33.80 \par USD/PHP    44.53-44.67      44.44-44.84 \par USD/IDR   13,150-13,200    13,060-13,300 \par USD/INR    63.63-63.89      63.36-64.16 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation higher. USD/CNY is still in a consolidation range spanning 6.1990-6.2104, largely ignoring the recent rise of the U.S. dollar index - which has however been pushing up the daily USD/CNY benchmark rate set by the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 . The yuan's movements have been muted in the spot market likely due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce volatility. At 0145 GMT the HSBC \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Flash manufacturing PMI for May will be released; a reading above last month's final reading of 48.9 may help stocks and the yuan, though it could be argued that an overly positive reading could have the opposite effect as punters might then reduce bullish bets on the possibility of less monetary policy easing and economic stimulus measures ahead. Overnight, \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields subsided - which might crimp the U.S. dollar's broad advance - as the minutes of the U.S. Federal Reserve's last policy meeting revealed a reluctance to raise interest rates in June. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 6.1990 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1934 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.2047 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 6.2104 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2133 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--downtrend may end. USD/TWD may soon rise out of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel as the higher intraday lows this week indicates buying on dips is prevalent. The U.S. dollar index has been rising steadily, though it lost steam overnight after the minutes of the U.S. Federal Reserve's last policy meeting revealed a reluctance to raise interest rates in June; most analysts still peg a U.S. rate hike in September or December. The offshore USD/TWD market has turned mildly bullish on USD/TWD as seen by the price of the 1-month nondeliverable forward contract rising above that of the spot contract - from a previous discount. In the background, the euro remains heavy, thus keeping the U.S. dollar supported, as Greece debt woes may come to a boil. Later today, Greek politicians will submit another budget restructuring proposal to the Eurogroup ministers in order to unlock more financial aid - failing which it might not make its next debt repayment to the \uc2 IMF\uc2 . \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.650 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.580 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support and base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.500 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.800 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 30.940 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.000 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--uptrend. The overnight surge of USD/JPY, coupled with growing Greek debt concerns, might push USD/KRW past the 1,100 round-figure trading barrier but the pair may stall at the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 1,103. The daily Bollinger uptrend channel - a bullish chart signal for USD/KRW - will remain in effect if the pair closes Thursday above 1,093. The U.S. dollar is likely to be well-supported as markets await the outcome of Greece's attempt - later today - to get the Eurogroup to approve its revised budget restructuring plan so as to unlock funding for looming debt repayments. Traders may also be influenced by the upcoming HSBC China flash manufacturing PMI for May at 0145GMT; a reading above last month's final print of 48.9 may help boost risk-taking sentiment and thereby smother the U.S. dollar. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,093 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,090 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,084 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is 1,100 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,103 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 1,107 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--uptrend. USD/SGD has crept into the Bollinger uptrend channel but the bullish bias may be tentative as the market awaits the HSBC China flash manufacturing PMI for May due at 0145GMT; a reading above last month's final print of 48.9 may help boost risk-taking sentiment and thereby smother the U.S. dollar. But if USD/SGD ends Thursday above 1.3345 the uptrend channel will be ratified and there will be a strong chance that the pair keeps climbing in the days ahead, targeting the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that hovers at around 1.3550-1.3600. The U.S. dollar index's rally slowed slightly overnight due to the minutes of the U.S. Federal Reserve's last policy meeting revealing that a June rate hike is off the table - which wasn't news to the market, really, since analysts mostly expect a rate increase in September or December. But the greenback may find support from a wilting euro that has been hammered by growing Greek debt concerns. Later today, the Greek government will seek approval for its latest budget reform plans in order to unlock funding from the Troika for looming debt repayments. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.3345 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.3300 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.3284 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is 1.3400 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.3407 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.3450 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside limited. USD/MYR entered the daily Bollinger uptrend channel on Wednesday, increasing bullish potential for the pair, but upside may be limited by the ceiling of the channel converging with the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone near 3.6340 thus creating a strong technical barrier. The U.S. dollar index made more headway overnight, though at a slower pace, as the minutes of the U.S. Federal Reserve's last policy meeting revealed a reluctance to raise interest rates in June. The next catalyst for volatility may come from the \uc2 HSBC\uc2  flash China manufacturing PMI for May due at 0145GMT - which may show that the economy is still contracting; last month's final reading of 48.9 was below the 50.0 watermark. A very weak number could fuel speculation of more China monetary policy easing - which might boost risk appetite and thus dampen the safe haven U.S. dollar in Asia. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.6040 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.6000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 3.5830 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.6340 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 3.6500 (psychological resistance), before 3.6700 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--possible uptrend. USD/THB is showing a mild bullish bias as it mimics the recent overnight movements of the benchmark ICE U.S. dollar index. A Thursday close above 33.65 would activate the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that could encourage short-term traders to buy, thus increasing technical momentum. Overnight, the U.S. dollar index rose for a third day as investors continued to fret over a potential Greek debt default. The Greek government will meet with the Eurogroup ministers later today to seek approval for its budget restructuring plans - failing which, financial aid will be withheld and Greece may not meet its upcoming debt repayment obligations to the \uc2 IMF\uc2 . Meanwhile, the dovish rhetoric of the Thai government on interest rates appears to be nudging \uc2 the Bank of Thailand\uc2  toward another interest rate cut - another factor that is positive for USD/THB. Thailand's Q1 gross domestic product data published Monday showed a slower-than-expected expansion of 3.0% versus forecasts for 3.4%. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 33.50 (psychological support), then at 33.29 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 33.20 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 33.65 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 33.80 (psychological resistance), before 34.00 (round-figure trading barrier and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--possible uptrend. USD/PHP may attempt to climb into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 44.67 after another overnight rise of the U.S. dollar index. A Thursday close above that level would confirm a bullish technical bias for USD/PHP that could lead the pair toward 45.00. Though the U.S. Federal Reserve projected a slightly dovish tone in its April meeting minutes - released Wednesday - the ongoing Greek debt debacle continues to weigh on EUR/USD and thus support the U.S. dollar broadly. At 0145 GMT the HSBC China flash manufacturing PMI for May will be released, and could spark volatility in regional markets if the numbers are far off from last month's final reading of 48.9. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.53 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone), then at 44.50 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 44.44 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 44.40 (200-day moving average line). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.67 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 44.84 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 20 May 2015 20:22 ET  USD/Asia Bullish Before Greek Debt Meeting -- -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--uptrend. USD/IDR has re-entered the daily Bollinger uptrend channel and may hence be heading higher once again. The overnight rise of the U.S. dollar index - despite a mildly dovish tone from the U.S. Federal Reserve's latest meeting minutes - ought to propel USD/IDR higher. The safe haven greenback continues to rise as risk aversion attributed to Greek debt default concerns keeps EUR/USD pinned down. Later today, the Greek government will seek approval for its latest budget reform plans in order to unlock funding from the Troika for looming debt repayments. Failure to get its new proposal approved would sink the euro because it would mean a likely Greek debt default in the weeks ahead. Another external factor that might move USD/IDR is the release of China's \uc2 HSBC\uc2  Flash manufacturing PMI at 0145 GMT; a reading far off from last month's final print of 48.9 could trigger a reaction in regional markets. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 13,150 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 13,060 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 13,020 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 13,200 (psychological resistance), then at 13,235 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 13,300 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--possible uptrend. USD/INR is currently propped up by the 20-day Bollinger mid line at 63.63 but may rally into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 63.89 with the benchmark U.S. dollar index rising a third day. The greenback is well-supported due to euro weakness ahead of another Greek debt negotiation meeting later today. Failure to get its new budget reform proposal approved by the Eurogroup ministers would sink the euro, and thereby rally the greenback, because it would mean that additional financial aid will be withheld and a Greek debt default could be imminent. Also on the investors' radars is the HSBC China flash manufacturing PMI for May; a reading far off from last months' final print of 48.9 could trigger regional market volatility as it would affect expectations of further China monetary policy easing. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 63.63 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 63.36 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 63.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 63.89 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 64.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 64.16 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 20, 2015 20:22 ET (00:22 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150521eb5l0000d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
