\par\par \b \uc2 China Hopes Strong Stock Market Can Stem Capital Outflows -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,836 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2015\par 07:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0535 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] China's policy makers are hoping that a more robust stock market will help offset capital outflows, says Shen Jianguang of \uc2 Mizuho Securities\uc2 . The economist says that while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cut in the bank reserve requirement on Sunday was designed to help economic fundamentals, it also shows the government wants to avoid a deep stock market correction. "In our view a 100 basis-point cut reflects the government's efforts to stabilize the stock market, following a sharp decline in A-share futures on Friday after the \uc2 China Securities Regulatory Commission\uc2  announced a clamp down on the use of margin-trading financing for equity purchases and increased the supply of shares available for short sellers." Despite strong trade surpluses, China had a drop of $110 billion in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the Jan-March period. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sunday cut the bank reserve requirement ratio by one percentage point, its biggest reduction since late 2008.\par \par \uc2  China's economic growth in the first quarter was a disappointing 7% year on year, the slowest pace in six years. (william.kazer@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0533 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Investors may find it hard to move this week with many sitting on sidelines ahead of the FOMC and the BOJ policy meeting next week, says Yuzo Sakai, manager of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  business promotion at Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  & Ueda Harlow. "The strength of a higher dollar is now taking a breather," says Mr. Sakai, adding that many expect the USD/JPY (now at 118.72) to trade in a 118-121 range over the short term. "If there is any motion, that would be the next week or the week later when speculative positions from overseas investors may kick in" to intentionally move the market at a time when liquidity remains thin and many Japanese investors are away on the Golden week holiday in early May.(hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor SXS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0533 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The NZD/USD is modestly higher late Monday after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  announced a 100 bps cut to the RRR for all banks, to 18.5%, and introduced restrictions on margin lending over the weekend, says RBC Fixed Income and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Strategist Michael Turner. He says the move by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is mildly positive for risk appetite and this had supported both the AUD/USD and the NZD/USD and allowed the NZD/USD to shrug off a soft 1Q CPI number. The NZD/USD is currently trading at 0.7703 vs 0.7698 early this morning in New Zealand. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com;Twitter: @lucy_craymer) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0506 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Hong Kong equities bobbed and weaved through the morning session as markets digested a weekend full of policy announcements from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Securities Regulatory Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  (CSRC). "The surprise announcement of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy easing after the CSRC move clearly shows that the authorities in Beijing prefer to control the pace of the remarkable rally in A-shares... while avoiding abrupt market dislocation that could complicate their (more important) growth stabilization efforts," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lombard Odier\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Nevertheless, early gains prove brittle and the market is down at the noon break. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index falls 0.3% to 27,571.60, while H-shares are flat; the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  China Enterprises Index holds steady at 14,541.57. (gregor.hunter@wsj.com; Twitter @gregorhunter) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: DWT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0455 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nikon\f28 \uc2 \f2  (7731.TO) are down 1.1% at Y1,691 after a Societe General downgrade to Sell from Buy. House Analyst Steve Myers cites the company's IC wafer scanner business which is "worse than expected" and "unlikely to improve" in the current FY ending next March, while the benefits expected from a richer mix of SLR cameras, and a gain of SLR market share, seem long gone. Accordingly, he cuts his target price from Y2,083 to Y1,450. Further negative catalysts potentially include further digital SLR market shrinkage, price erosion, or loss of share by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nikon\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a weakening of demand for TVs or premium smartphone displays feeding through to sale of fewer flat panel display tools than management expects, and potentially less favorable foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates, he adds. "IC wafer scanner sales may not decline further but upside appears limited," he says. (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: DWT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0436 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Chinese households will pump more of their savings into the stock market over the next three years, Nomura says in a bullish forecast. Chinese families could boost the amount of their savings in stocks from 17% at the end of 2014 to nearly 30% in 2017 while they decrease the proportion deposited in banks--a shift pouring nearly 22.5 trillion yuan into equities. "Starry-eyed" first-time investors, including white-collar young professionals, migrant workers and service sector workers, have also eagerly piled into the market, Nomura says. Their numbers helped jack up the boom of more than 1.6 million new stock trading accounts at the end of March. Figures could rise even higher, as Chinese investors looking to buy shares from initial public offerings open extra accounts under the names of family and friends to increase the odds of a bigger allotment.(dominique.fong@wsj.com; Twitter: @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0433 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Malaysia is seeing a steady growth in medical tourism. Last year, 800,000 tourists visited the country for medical reasons--such as cardiology, fertility, dentistry, neurology, orthopaedic and ophthalmologic to Malaysia Healthcare Travel Council (MHTC) an agency under the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ministry of Health\f28 \uc2 \f2 . That is up 37% from 583,000 in 2011. Revenue earned from those visits rose 43% to MYR730 million ($201 million) last year from MYR509.77 million in 2011. This year 1 million tourists are expected to enter the country to seek medical treatment, bringing with them an estimated MYR1 billion, the ministry says. According to consultants Frost & Sullivan, Thailand and Singapore will continue to see higher revenue numbers, but they are forecast to see slower growth over the next five years, compared with Malaysia's forecast compound annual growth rate of 18.5% between 2014 and 2020. It said "Malaysia has the opportunity to brand and position itself as a provider of affordable, quality healthcare."(celine.fernandez@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0428 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] As resources investment declines, investors are watching to see if Australia's economy to rebalance. But rebalance to what? \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  says that while manufacturing is the instinctive response, the answer is more likely to be the services sector, which accounts for roughly 75% of Australia's gross domestic product. Services exports should rise thanks in part to rising Asian middle class incomes, economists \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paul Bloxham\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Daniel Smith say. A lower Aussie dollar should also lift exports while at the same time discouraging Australians from spending as much on services from abroad, they say. The services sector was the strongest contributor to employment growth over the past year. (robb.stewart@wsj.com; Twitter: @RobbMStewart) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0427 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it expects Indian property developers to be able to lower their debt "meaningfully" by the end of 2016 as India's investment climate improves. The process of reducing debt had stalled in 2014 due to weak sales and slower cash collections on properties that were sold towards the end of 2014 and in early 2015, as developers introduced easy payment schemes to stoke demand, says the ratings firm. Fitch says domestic property purchases remained weak in 2014 due to high interest rates and some political and policy uncertainty in an election year. Buyers postponed their purchases, which drove up inventory levels steadily during the last 12 months, it says. Fitch expects the property development sector to be a key beneficiary of cuts in housing loan interest rates by several domestic banks in April 2015 following rate reductions by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (kenan.machado@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0420 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Chinese banks are the key beneficiaries as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's bigger-than-expected reserve requirement ratio (RRR) cut releases more than 1 trillion yuan into the banking system, say analysts. "We believe the RRR cut should help maintain ample system liquidity, thereby lowering the event and perceived asset quality risks of Chinese banks," says Deutsche, which maintains its bullish view on Chinese banks. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  adds that the RRR cut could boost profit before tax by 1% on average for Chinese banks. The move will also give the banks ample capital to participate in the upcoming local government bond issuance, it says. Chinese banks generally rise Monday with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agricultural Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1288.HK), up 2.5%, leading the gains. (jacky.wong@wsj.com; Twitter: @jackycwong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0414 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2 's latest aggressive move to cut the reserve requirement ratio--the second time this year--is a response to continuing capital outflows and further deceleration in the country's economic growth, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. It says an RRR cut releases longer-term liquidity, lowers banks' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  costs (with the benefit likely to be passed on to borrowers), and provides a strong signal that the government intends to use available policy space to achieve its growth targets. The bank expects \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely cut the benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points by end-June to lower its cost of capital. Moreover, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is prepared to sell \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent significant Chinese yuan depreciation, and would cut the RRR further, if necessary, to offset the loss of domestic liquidity due to such an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the bank adds. It says \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economic growth may revive in the second half, supported by policy easing. (chester.yung@wsj.com; Twitter: @chester_yung) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 20 Apr 2015 01:35 ET \par China Hopes Strong Stock Market Can Stem Capital -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0401 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/IDR is up slightly at 12,875 from its Friday close of 12,845, implying a marginally weaker rupiah versus the U.S. dollar. USD/IDR, unlike some other USD/Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pairs in the region, has not reacted to the improvement in risk-taking sentiment following China's surprise move Sunday to ease bank-lending limits. The safe-haven greenback has slipped against most other Southeast Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the Philippine peso and the Singapore dollar. However, the bearish USD/IDR chart bias will remain if it closes Monday below 12,895 and thus inside the Bollinger downtrend channel. A daily close below 12,795--under the base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone--would intensify the bearish signal. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 20, 2015 01:35 ET (05:35 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150420eb4k000ex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
