\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China says to accelerate reforms to support yuan in \uc2 IMF \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  basket\b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2015\par 21:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (changes dateline to WASHINGTON; updates with Zhou comments to \uc2 IMF\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, April 18 (Reuters) - Beijing will accelerate reforms to the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of a push for the yuan's inclusion in the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2  said on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  steering committee, Zhou argued that Beijing had made strides toward making the yuan freely convertible, and that it should be included in the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's Special Drawing Rights basket.\par \par \uc2 China has committed to further open its capital account and liberalize the way the exchange rate for the yuan, or RMB, is managed, including reducing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not far from achieving its goal of RMB capital account convertibility," Zhou said.\par \par \uc2 Winning approval for the yuan's inclusion in the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket could raise China's standing in the global financial system and mark an important step in Beijing's emergence as a global power.\par \par \uc2 The United States, the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's top shareholder, has said China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not yet ready to join the SDR basket. A top \uc2 IMF\uc2  official said China does not want to bend the rules in its favor.\par \par \uc2 Zhou had earlier commented on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform push in an interview with \uc2 Xinhua\uc2  reporters in Washington on Friday, where he was attending a meeting of the \uc2 IMF\uc2 . (Reporting by Jason Lange in Washington; Additional reporting by Pete Sweeney and David Lin in Shanghai; Editing by Jeremy Laurence and Tim Ahmann) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-18T20:35:49.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150418eb4i00iod\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
