\par\par \b \uc2 Half of China's total trade to be settled in yuan by 2020-\uc2 HSBC\uc2  CEO\b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 06:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, March 26 (Reuters) - Cross-border trade settlement denominated in China's yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to climb to over 50 percent of China's total trade by 2020, more than doubling the current level, \uc2 Stuart Gulliver\uc2 , \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's Group Chief Executive, said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A scheme launched in 2009 and initially in five Chinese cities to encourage cross-border trade settlement in yuan rather than U.S. dollars has seen rapid growth in the past few years, with yuan settlement of trade debts rising from 1 percent of transactions in 2010 to 22 percent last year.\par \par \uc2 This robust momentum was not affected by the quick depreciation of the yuan earlier this year, showing the yuan's use in trade settlement is rooted in genuine need and supported by confidence in the fundamental and relative stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Gulliver told a forum in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 The yuan, nicknamed the "redback", fell 2.4 percent against the dollar in 2014 and that weakness remained until earlier this month when suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped it recover some ground.\par \par \uc2 So far, the geographical spread of China's trading partners denominating trade in the yuan remains very narrow, with the lion's share taking place in Hong Kong and most of the rest happening elsewhere in Asia.\par \par \uc2 "In this sense, the renminbi (yuan) is not yet as integrated as a trade \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it both could be and will be. We do expect this to change," said Gulliver.\par \par \uc2 China's yuan has already broken into the top five as an international payments \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , overtaking the Canadian dollar and the Australian dollar, said global transaction services organisation SWIFT.\par \par \uc2 Gulliver expected the yuan to increasingly represent a viable alternative to the U.S. dollar and to finally become a main reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  alongside with the U.S. dollar and the euro. (Reporting by \uc2 Michelle Chen\uc2 ; Editing by Eric Meijer) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-26T06:18:48.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150326eb3q005pl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
