\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fed uncertainties support Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ;  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  manufacturing survey weighs\b0\par\par\uc2 790 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 06:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won up on exporters; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution limits gains\par     * Rupiah rises on NDFs, bond prices up\par     * Ringgit advances on higher stocks, bonds\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, March 24 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  extended gains on Tuesday in the uncertainty over the\par timing of U.S. interest rate hikes, while a gloomy survey of\par China's manufacturing sector dimmed the appeal of some regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     South Korea's won and Indonesia's rupiah \par rose to their highest in more than two weeks. The Malaysian\par ringgit advanced with higher stocks and bonds prices.\par     The dollar on Monday broadly fell on views that the U.S.\par Federal Reserve will not hurry to raise interest rates. Low U.S.\par borrowing costs are usually seen to boost the attractiveness of\par higher yields in emerging Asia.\par     Still, \f28 \uc2 \f2 San Francisco Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Williams\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Fed\par policymakers should wait no more than a few months before\par considering raising interest rates. He also said the U.S.\par economy is strong enough to handle a firm dollar.\par   \par     Activity in China's factory sector slid to an 11-month low\par in March as new orders shrank, a private survey showed,\par indicating the economy may need more policy stimulus.\par  \par     Many Asian central banks have already eased monetary\par policies to tackle slowing economies and inflation.\par     "Don't go chasing the waterfall," said Andy Ji, Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Singapore, when asked if emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par appreciate further.\par     "USD/Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are still 'buy on the dips' into the\par Fed's normalization. Concerns over capital flight, a more\par entrenched easing bias, and a generally more sluggish outlook in\par the domestic economies should keep USD/Asia well supported."\par     \par     WON\par     The won advanced as much as 0.8 percent to 1,105.4 per\par dollar, its strongest since March 6, on month-end demand from\par exporters for settlements.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gave up some of earlier gains as\par caution grew over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities to stem its appreciation.\par     Local importers also bought dollars for payments, limiting\par the won's upside, traders said.\par     The won is seen facing a chart resistance at 1,104.3, the 50\par percent Fibonacci retracement of its depreciation between\par January and March, analysts said.\par     If the resistance in broken, the next levels would be\par 1,099.9, a 55-day moving average, and 1,098.3, a 100-day\par average, they added.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah gained as much as 0.5 percent to 12,950 per\par dollar, its strongest since March 6.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened in non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs) markets, while the government bond\par prices rose.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 12,972 rupiah per dollar,\par stronger than Monday's 13,076.\par     The rupiah pared some of its earlier gains on month-end\par corporate dollar demand.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit rose as Malaysia's government bond prices gained\par  and Kuala Lumpur shares outperformed peers in Southeast\par Asia.\par     Five-year bond yield fell to 3.622 percent, its\par lowest since March 2.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of its earlier gains as\par oil prices dropped after the sluggish China manufacturing\par survey.   Malaysia is a net oil exporter and sliding crude\par prices increased concerns that its current account surplus may\par fall and its fiscal deficit may widen.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0440 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.67         119.73       +0.05\par   Sing dlr        1.3679         1.3649       -0.22\par   Taiwan dlr      31.350         31.503       +0.49\par   Korean won     1106.35        1114.60       +0.75\par   Baht             32.55          32.55       +0.00\par   Peso             44.74          44.79       +0.11\par   Rupiah        12965.00       13014.00       +0.38\par   Rupee            62.20          62.27       +0.11\par   Ringgit         3.6700         3.6950       +0.68\par   Yuan            6.2122         6.2160       +0.06\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan 