\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar's resilience hurts Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , weekly regional gains seen\b0\par\par\uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 06:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Ringgit at 6-yr low, Malaysian inflation lowest in 5 yrs\par     * Rupiah falls on month-end corporate dollar demand\par     * Yuan leads weekly Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, March 20 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased on Friday, hurt by the dollar's overnight\par rebound, but regional units were set to see weekly gains on a\par dovish stance by the U.S. Federal Reserve, with China's yuan on\par the course for its best week in a decade.\par     Malaysia's ringgit hit a six-year low after data\par showing February inflation was the weakest in more than five\par years. \par     The Indonesian rupiah fell on month-end dollar\par demand from local companies such as importers.\par     South Korea's won slid on caution over possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem its\par strength against the yen.\par     The Philippine peso hit a two-month low as\par offshore funds sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in overnight non-deliverable\par forwards markets.\par     The dollar slid against a basket of six major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but stayed well above this week's lows touched as\par the Fed was seen in no rush to raise interest rates after this\par week's policy meeting. \par     The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is still expected to increase\par borrowing costs this year.\par     "USD waxes and wanes but market participants remain split on\par Fed's policy path. This means lingering uncertainty and higher\par USD/Asia," said Andy Ji, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\par     Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have fallen so far this year\par as higher U.S. borrowing costs will likely hurt attractiveness\par of higher yields in the region.\par     \par     YUAN'S BEST WEEK IN DECADE\par     Most regional units, however, were to set to post weekly\par gains as the Fed's policy comments this week eased expectations\par of an early rate hike in June.\par     The yuan led the way with a 1.2 percent rise\par against the dollar so far this week, its sharpest rise since its\par landmark revaluation in 2005, Thomson Reuters data showed. The\par weekly gain helped the renminbi reverse losses so far this year.\par     That came as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while setting a series of\par stronger midpoints. The authority was seen fighting against the\par risk off capital flight and speculation for further\par depreciation. \par     Short positions in the yuan were reduced in the last two\par weeks while sentiment towards regional peers deteriorated, a\par Reuters poll showed on Thursday. \par     The Taiwan dollar has risen 0.8 percent so far this\par week on stock inflows.\par     The rupiah has appreciated 0.8 percent with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suffered a\par fifth consecutive weekly loss.\par     India's rupee and Thailand's baht have\par risen 0.7 percent each. The won has risen 0.6 percent. \par     The peso and the ringgit bucked against weekly regional\par appreciation.\par     The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost 1.2 percent so far this\par week, which would be its largest weekly loss since March 2014,\par as offshore funds sold it amid lower bond prices.\par     The ringgit has fallen 1.0 percent on concerns over a\par possible downgrade in credit ratings amid worries that low oil\par prices may widen Malaysia's fiscal deficit.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0455 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       120.69         120.79       +0.08\par   Sing dlr        1.3878         1.3874       -0.03\par   Taiwan dlr      31.450         31.502       +0.17\par   Korean won     1121.60        1117.20       -0.39\par   Baht             32.69          32.73       +0.12\par   Peso             44.84          44.72       -0.27\par   Rupiah        13090.00       13030.00       -0.46\par   Rupee            62.55          62.52       -0.05\par   Ringgit         3.7230         3.7055       -0.47\par   Yuan            6.1875         6.1961       +0.14\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       120.69         119.66       -0.86\par   Sing dlr        1.3878         1.3260       -4.45\par   Taiwan dlr      31.450         31.718    