\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan rebounds on strong midpoint, suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 05:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, March 17 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan is set for its\par biggest rise against the dollar in six weeks after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed a firmer midpoint on Tuesday.\par     Traders also reported that big Chinese state-owned banks\par massively sold dollars, possibly on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par to boost the value of the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     These bank moves have become increasingly conspicuous since\par early last week and may signal that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has low\par tolerance for a sharp depreciation in the yuan, traders said.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate\par  at 6.1585 per dollar prior to market open on Tuesday,\par firmer than the previous fix at 6.1615. \par     The spot market opened at 6.2587 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.2548 at midday, 76 pips firmer than the\par previous close.\par     Spot yuan, allowed to trade with a range 2 percent above or\par below the official fixing on any given day, was 1.56 percent\par weaker than the midpoint.\par     It approached the 2-percent daily limit nearly every day in\par early March before the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  intensified\par last week, traders said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been under heavy downward pressure since\par late 2014, hit by China's slowing economic growth and weakness\par in non-dollar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to control the pace of the yuan's\par depreciation, partly by using some big state-owned banks to sell\par dollars to set a floor for the downside, traders said.\par     "It shows the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's efforts to guide the yuan to\par fall only slowly," said a trader at a city commercial bank in\par Shanghai.\par     The yuan has depreciated at a slower pace against the dollar\par and thus gained value against a basket of trade-weighted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according to the Bank for International Settlement\par (BIS) index for the yuan's real effective exchange rate (REER),\par published late on Monday.\par     The BIS index for the yuan's REER - the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's value\par against a trade-weighted basket after adjustments based on\par inflation - hit a record high and rose 1.29 percent to 130.37 in\par February. \par     The yuan has eased only 0.6 percent against the dollar so\par far this year, in sharp contrast to losses in other major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including the euro and yen, as the dollar index\par  rallied to a 12-year high last week.\par     Offshore yuan was trading 0.09 percent weaker than onshore\par spot at 6.2602 per dollar on Tuesday.\par     \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item                           Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint                  6.1585   6.1615    0.05%\par  Spot yuan                      6.2548   6.2624    0.12%\par  Divergence from midpoint*      1.56%              \par  Spot change ytd                                   -0.81%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                32.32%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument                      Current   Difference\par                                            from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan        *     6.2602    -0.09%\par  Offshore non-deliverable        6.3995    -3.77%\par  forwards               **                 \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Jacqueline\par Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-17T05:43:37.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150317eb3h0053f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
