\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan nearly flat amid suspected c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 05:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, March 11 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan barely moved\par against the dollar on Wednesday as large state-owned banks were\par suspected to have sold dollars to support the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par possibly on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     For many years the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 has been\par known to use state banks to help adjust dollar supply and demand\par in the domestic market and help achieve Beijing's targets for\par the yuan's exchange rate.\par     Since mid-2014, however, it has sharply reduced its daily\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders say.\par     "Of late, we again feel the 'force' that is helping maintain\par the stability of the market," said a trader at a city commercial\par bank in Shanghai, referring to the suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     While the market has never been able to tell exactly whether\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on specific days, traders typically\par sense the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's invisible hand by identifying\par large-scale \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by government-controlled banks, they have\par said.\par     On Wednesday, the spot market opened at 6.2635\par per dollar and was changing hands at 6.2622 at midday, only 2\par pips weaker from the previous close.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1597 per\par dollar prior to market open, weaker than the previous fix of\par 6.1572. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade with a range\par 2 percent above or below the official fixing on any given day.\par     It was the fifth consecutive day that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par weakened its daily guidance rate, sending it to the lowest level\par since early November on Wednesday.\par     The series of weaker \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  fixings reflect the strength of\par the U.S. dollar index, which has appreciated almost 10\par percent this year to a nearly 12-year high on Tuesday, exerting\par greater depreciation pressure on the yuan. \par     While the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has used the official rate to signal\par its tolerance of gradual yuan depreciation, traders do not\par believe it will allow a sharp fall as China is facing pressure\par from capital outflows.\par     China posted a record $91.2 billion deficit on its capital\par and financial account last quarter, the biggest quarterly\par deficit since the quarterly data was published in 1998.\par (Graphic: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qeq24w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qeq24w}}}\uc2 \f2 )\par     For 2014, it had a $96 billion deficit on the account, the\par record annual outflows since data was available in 1982.\par (Graphic: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/kyt24w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/kyt24w}}}\uc2 \f2 )\par     On Wednesday, The offshore yuan was trading 0.18 percent\par weaker than the onshore spot at 6.2736 per dollar. \par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item                        Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1597   6.1572    -0.04%\par  Spot yuan                   6.2622   6.262     0.00%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   1.66%              \par  Spot change ytd                                -0.93%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation             32.17%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument                   Current   Difference\par                                         from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan        *  6.2736    -0.18%\par  Offshore non-deliverable     6.4045    -3.82%\par  forwards               **              \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-11T05:25:42.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150311eb3b0053l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
