\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's Yuan Ends up as  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Seen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  -2-\b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 10:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                   Vs Parity    Pvs \par USD/CNY Central Parity   6.1572               6.1563 \par USD/CNY OTC 0830 GMT     6.2620     1.70%     6.2644 \par              High        6.2643     1.74% \par              Low         6.2610     1.69% \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI--China's yuan ended slightly higher against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seen discreetly defending its own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  despite the greenback's global strength.\f28 \par \par \uc2 On the over-the-counter market, the dollar closed at CNY6.2620, down from Monday's close of CNY6.2644. It traded narrowly between CNY6.2610 and CNY6.2643.\par \par \uc2 "The authorities appeared to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market while the yuan's reference exchange rate was rather steady," said a trader with an Asian bank.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set the dollar-yuan central-parity rate, a reference exchange rate, at 6.1572, up from 6.1563 the previous day.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently wants to maintain stability in the market while the National People's Congress is still going on," said the trader, referring to the annual meetings of China's legislative body.\par \par \uc2 "Things will change once the meetings are over," the trader added.\par \par \uc2 Offshore, one-year dollar/yuan nondeliverable forward contracts were at CNY6.4045, compared with CNY6.4005 late Monday.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore yuan market in Hong Kong, where the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats freely, the dollar was at CNY6.2750, versus CNY6.2734 late Monday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Shen Hong at hong.shen@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 10-03-15 0913GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150310eb3a000br\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
