\par\par \b \uc2 Cheaper Yuan? Foreign  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Deposits Surged In China -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shuli Ren   \par \uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 08:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Anticipating a rising U.S. dollar and a cheaper yuan, people put record amount of their money into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts in China.\par \par \uc2 In January, total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits in China surged by $82.3 billion to $655.7 billion, the largest monthly increase since this data series collected by the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  began in 2009. For comparison purposes, for the entire year of 2014, the increase was only $134 billion.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the yuan. Net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases fell again in January, dropped $17.4 billion following December's $19.1 billion decline.\par \par \uc2 The pressure on yuan is not likely to abate soon. After all, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is moving the opposite direction from the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 . US is still expected to raise rates later this year, while China is expected to cut rates again. It makes no sense for China to artificially prop up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially considering yuan is now a lot more expensive than yen and the Euro.\par \par \uc2 But the yuan depreciation is likely to be slow and steady, argued \uc2 Barclays\uc2 . One of the key reasons is the hot money outflow. Here are analysts Dennis Tan and Mitul Kotecha:\par \par \uc2 We remain of the view that China will accommodate further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness in a gradual fashion (we forecast USDCNY at 6.40 by year-end), through a combination of weaker CNY fixings and possibly a widening of the trading band. However, the recent surge in capital outflows probably means that Chinese authorities have become even more cautious about fuelling CNY depreciation expectations in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Year-to-date, the yuan has lost 1% against the dollar. The iShares China Large Cap ETF ( FXI) has gained only 0.2% and the \uc2 iShares MSCI China ETF\uc2  ( MCHI) has advanced 1.9%.\par \par \uc2 More at Barron's Asia Stocks to Watch blog, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/asiastocks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/asiastocks/}}}\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Barclays Plc\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=GB0031348658"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=GB0031348658}}}\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Barclays Plc\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US06738E2046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US06738E2046}}}\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Barclays Plc\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=GB0031348658"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=GB0031348658}}}\par \par \uc2 Access Investor Kit for \uc2 Barclays Plc\par \par \uc2 Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US06738E2046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.companyspotlight.com/partner?cp_code=P479&isin=US06738E2046}}}\par \par \uc2