\par\par \b \uc2 Investors Brace For Potential Yuan Depreciation\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chiara Albanese   \par \uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2015\par 07:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Should investors now be worried about the falling yuan?\par \par \uc2 For years the Chinese authorities guided the yuan higher, helping draw in cash and fuel economic growth. However, the yuan has recently fallen to the lower end of its government-defined trading band, and institutional investors who have been adding this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and yuan-denominated bonds, to their investment strategies are now being forced to consider the possibility of Beijing addressing slowing growth by devaluing.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has lost about 0.8% so far this year, after falling 2.4% last year, which was the biggest drop for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2005.\par \par \uc2 "As an investor having positions in A-shares, [yuan] depreciation means a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  loss for us. We need to take this risk into account," said Haiyan Li Labbe, China analyst at French asset manager Carmignac, which has been granted a specific licence to invest in shares and Chinese bonds denominated in yuan.\par \par \uc2 The firm is considering buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options to protect the portfolio from further depreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This could well be needed as Carmignac forecasts a 3% fall in the yuan against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to limit yuan's depreciation. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs a relatively solid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it's promoting the yuan's internationalization and it's trying to attract more foreign investors," said Ms. Li Labbe.\par \par \uc2 Paresh Upadhyaya, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Pioneer Investments\uc2  in Boston shares a bearish outlook for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last year was the first year the yuan depreciated against the dollar since the end of the de facto peg in July 2005. "This marks a significant turning point for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A record outflow in the country's balance of payments is adding to the downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Mr. Upadhyaya said. The\par \par \uc2 The falling yuan "is altering foreign investment opportunities in China. I expect another modest depreciation in the yuan versus the dollar in 2015, likely to be larger than 2014," Mr. Upadhyaya added.\par \par \uc2 However, not everyone is convinced the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bad times ahead.\par \par \uc2 "A weaker renminbi would be inconsistent with a correction in global imbalances and this makes no sense for China or the rest of the world," said Andy Seaman, partner and chief investment officer at Stratton Street LLP.\par \par \uc2 London-based Stratton Street launched, in November 2007, a renminbi bond fund for international investors which can own dim sum issues or investment grade hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds hedged back to the yuan. The firm has $1.1 billion assets under management, and is hedged against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure.\par \par \uc2 "So while it might make sense for the Chinese to widen the band to make the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexible we would doubt if any such move would be to facilitate depreciation. In fact, such widening is far more likely to occur when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is towards the top of the band as this reduces the need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , building up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, something they have stated as undesirable given the already substantial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves," said Mr. Seaman.\par \par \uc2 If anything, investors should be more concerned about capital inflows driving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stronger, rather than worrying about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness, Mr Seaman added.\par \par \uc2 In addition, Raymond Gui, portfolio manager at Income Partners Asset Management believes the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to maintain a relatively stable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, as they did during the 1997 Asian Financial Crisis and 2008 subprime crisis.\par \par \uc2 "A sharp depreciation in renminbi is against China's interest, as it could potentially trigger huge capital outflows, which would override any potential effect of stimulating exports," he said. "Investors should also look at the much higher carry of the yuan versus the dollar and other major hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Income Partners currently manages $1.3 billion of assets as of the end of December 2014.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 19-02-15 0655GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150219eb2j0001p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
