\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan Strength Vs EM  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  to Curb China Exports -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 143 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2015\par 04:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0314 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The yuan has been rising against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other emerging economies despite its weakness against the U.S. dollar, and this will likely put pressure on China's exporters this year, economists at Capital Economics say. The research house cited U.S. data as showing that prices of imports from China have remained stable in dollar terms while prices from other emerging economies have been falling. "In recent weeks, the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan from weakening. [The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] will come under pressure to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slide if exports start to suffer," its economists say in a note to clients. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Editor: KLH\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 27-01-15 0326GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150127eb1r0004d\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (china near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw)and (central bank o